nistic turnId rather than recreating\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:489:  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:536:    turns: DerivedTurn[];\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:543:  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:566:Trusted callers supply already-finalized archive-entry payloads to the durable\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:567:append/read primitive. Convex owns the canonical row shape, taxonomy\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:575:    participant X as Convex archiveEntries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:589:`process-live.ts`. Those live messages are not archive writes. Only completed\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:604:This flow covers AC-3.1 through AC-3.4. The user reads archive entries through\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:608:returns archive response rows for the client surface to render.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:613:canonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:618:This flow covers AC-4.1 through AC-4.4. Turn derivation reads archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:619:in ascending `sequence`, groups them deterministically, and writes cached turns\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:624:1. `user_message` starts a new turn.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:625:2. Entries before the first user message form turn `0` if they exist.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:627:   `tool_result`, and `process_event` attach to the active turn.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:628:  4. A `tool_result` with `relatedToolCallId` stays in the same turn as its\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:630:  5. Degraded related context degrades the turn, not the archive entries.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:632:Rebuild behavior is explicit: Epic 7 rebuilds turns on turn/derived-view read\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:633:or explicit derived-view refresh, not on every archive append. Rebuild upserts by\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:634:stable `turnId` and `turnIndex`.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:639:turns, not from raw live state. The first slice produces:\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:641:- `turn_range`: one contiguous range of turn indexes with source entry ids\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:642:- `chunk_candidate`: a candidate grouping over one or more turns for future\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:651:ids. Building on the Flow 3 archive read surface, read services enrich when\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:660:the artifact/source lookup-failure degradation semantics: the archive entry\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:663:canonical entry. Story 3 remains responsible for rendering that response\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:666:### Flow 7: Return Later and Bound Long Reads\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:668:This flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:672:- archive entries: default 100, max 200\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:673:- turns: default 50, max 100\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:674:- derived views: default 50\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:676:A derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:677:return degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:684:| 0 | Foundation | Contracts, Convex schema, fixtures, error codes, compatibility mapping skeletons | All support | Relevant sections: API Contracts, Data Model. Non-TC: archive contract vocabulary and finalized-only schema test |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:686:| 2 | Finalization boundary | Completion hooks, live/archive separation, retry idempotency | AC-2.x | Relevant sections: Flow 2, Service Interfaces. Non-TC: live-history separation, compatibility mapping decision |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:687:| 3 | Archive read/reopen | Routes, access controls, empty state, bounded page contract, environment-loss reads, degraded-entry display | AC-3.x | Relevant sections: Flow 3, Route Validation. Non-TC: invalid archive request handling |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:688:| 4 | Turn derivation | Deterministic grouping, cached rebuild, degraded turns | AC-4.x | Relevant sections: Flow 4, Data Model. Non-TC: turn-zero grouping, rebuild stability |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:689:| 5 | Structural derived views | `turn_range`, `chunk_candidate`, refresh, degradation | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Route Validation. Non-TC: no generated summary body, stale/rebuilt derived views |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:706:| Historical migration/backfill from `processHistoryItems` | A7 | Epic 7 starts forward canonical archive and compatibility bridge | Later migration if needed |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
