ject-and-process-shell/stories/05-return-and-recovery-visibility.md:81:  - When: The user returns later and the project shell loads\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/05-return-and-recovery-visibility.md:85:  - When: The user returns later and the shell loads\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/05-return-and-recovery-visibility.md:89:  - When: The user returns later and the shell loads\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/05-return-and-recovery-visibility.md:96:  - When: User returns to that URL\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/05-return-and-recovery-visibility.md:110:| Get project shell data | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project identity plus project shell summaries |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/05-return-and-recovery-visibility.md:112:In Epic 1, the project shell read path returns all process summaries needed to render and validate project-level process selection. The selected process is derived from the current browser route and matched against the returned `processes.items` collection. This story depends on durable shell reads rather than any server-persisted selected-process write path.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/04-process-registration-in-a-project.md:145:**Success response:** `POST /api/projects/{projectId}/processes` returns `201` with a `Create Process Response` body.\\n./apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:50:    const turns = deriveTurnsFromArchiveEntries(entries, args.processId);\\n./apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:55:      turns,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:58:    return turns;\\n./tests/service/client/create-project-modal.test.ts:81:  it('TC-6.1a cancel project creation returns to a stable project index', () => {\\n./tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts:88:  it('TC-1.1a returns shell HTML for authenticated project route', async () => {\\n./tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts:174:  it('returns the authenticated user from /auth/me', async () => {\\n./tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts:574:          turns: [],\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:162:| Get project shell data | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project identity plus project shell summaries |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:164:In Epic 1, the project shell read path returns all process summaries needed to render and validate project-level process selection. The selected process is derived from the current browser route and matched against the returned `processes.items` collection. The shell read path may also return section-level error states for `processes`, `artifacts`, or `sourceAttachments` without failing the entire project-shell response when project identity and access still succeed. This story does not add a separate single-process read endpoint or a server-persisted selected-process write path.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:166:At Story 3 boundary, this is the first story that returns populated shell-section envelopes and section-level error states. Earlier stories may open the shell successfully without yet owning full summary population semantics.\\n./tests/service/server/local-provider-adapter.test.ts:142:  it('hydrateEnvironment fails fast when a source clone returns an error', async () => {\\n./tests/service/server/local-provider-adapter.test.ts:185:  it('executeScript runs a real Node script that writes a result file and returns the parsed ExecutionResult', async () => {\\n./tests/service/server/local-provider-adapter.test.ts:259:  it('executeScript returns a failed ExecutionResult when the runtime exits 