-derived-views/test-plan.md:84:| TC-7.1b | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | `TC-7.1b derived view restores after reload` | View readable or rebuilt |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:86:| TC-7.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-7.3a archive read returns bounded page` | Page has limit and next cursor |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:95:| `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | same `processId + finalizationKey` returns or no-ops existing archive row | Primitive idempotency guard below Story 2 service proofs |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:97:| `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` | turn-cache rebuild preserves stable turn provenance for derived views | Prevents dangling view references after rebuild |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:99:| `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | stale derived views are rebuilt from current turns without breaking archive reads | Covers rebuild consistency after new archive entries |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:101:| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | derived-view refresh conflict returns `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Error contract coverage |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:102:| `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | invalid archive query returns `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Error contract coverage |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:112:| 4 Turn derivation | 5 | 2 | 7 | turn derivation service |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:120:no-summary enforcement, stale/rebuilt derived views, primitive idempotency, atomic sequence\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:139:6. Open the turn view and verify turns reference source archive entries.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:140:7. Open derived views and verify structural turn ranges/chunk candidates have no generated summary text.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:6:process archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:8:history while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:31:entries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:41:| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:45:archive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:56:| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:61:| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:78:The design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:134:entries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:147:| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:176:├── turn-derivation.service.ts                # NEW: deterministic turn derivation and rebuild\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:190:├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:200:├── service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts    # NEW: deterministic turn derivation tests\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:202:├── service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts # NEW: turn surface rendering tests\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:211:| `convex/archiveTurns.ts` | New | Store rebuildable cached turns | Convex schema | AC-4.x, AC-7.1 |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:212:| `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts` | New | Store/read structural derived views | Convex schema | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:215:| `TurnDerivationService` | New | Deterministically derive/rebuild turns from archive entries | PlatformStore | AC-4.x |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:219:| Client archive sections | New | Render archive, turns, structural views, empty/degraded states | Shared contracts/API client | AC-3.x, AC-4.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:298:not canonical. `TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` must upsert turns by stable\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:330:summary content. Derived-view rows may be deleted and recreated from turns; this\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:334:bounded. Epic 7 limits turn rows to one process turn and derived views to small\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:409:| Get process turns | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns` | `TurnDerivationService.getTurns` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:429:| `GET /archive/turns` | `{ turns, page }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:480:  // Rebuilds cached turns by deterministic turnId rather than recreating\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:489:  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:536:    turns: DerivedTurn[];\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:543:  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:608:returns archive response rows for the client surface to render.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:619:in ascending `sequence`, groups them deterministically, and writes cached turns\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:632:Rebuild behavior is explicit: Epic 7 rebuilds turns on turn/derived-view read\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:639:turns, not from raw live state. The first slice produces:\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:642:- `chunk_candidate`: a candidate grouping over one or more turns for future\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:668:This flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:673:- turns: default 50, max 100\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:674:- derived views: default 50\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:688:| 4 | Turn derivation | Deterministic grouping, cached rebuild, degraded turns | AC-4.x | Relevant sections: Flow 4, Data Model. Non-TC: turn-zero grouping, rebuild stability |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:689:| 5 | Structural derived views | `turn_range`, `chunk_candidate`, refresh, degradation | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Route Validation. Non-TC: no generated summary body, stale/rebuilt derived views |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:724:- [x] Turns and derived views are rebuildable, not canonical.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:18:Deliver the package-export pipeline for reviewed package snapshots so the user can request a bounded archive from the same workspace. Export remains a two-phase flow in this story: POST returns signed metadata, then GET streams the archive. Until a downstream process-module epic publishes package snapshots in normal product flow, this story is exercised through tests and manual Convex seeding.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:55:  - Then: The platform returns a markdown package (`.mpkz`) export for that currently reviewed package\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:91:| Request package export | `POST` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}/export` | Phase 1 of export. Validates exportability, mints a signed download URL with bounded expiry, returns an `ExportPackageResponse` including `downloadUrl` and `expiresAt` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:92:| Download package export | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/exports/{exportId}` | Phase 2 of export. Consumes the signed token issued by the POST, re-verifies access and exportability, and streams the `.mpkz` archive as `application/gzip`. Returns `404 REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` when the token is expired, tampered, or missing |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:142:- Export preflight returns bounded signed-download metadata and the resulting archive name ends in `.mpkz`\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:4:archive, turn derivation, and derived archive views. It serves as the source of\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:17:turns or chunks did not replace the original process record.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:31:loss, and can be grouped into turns without mutating the archive. The first\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:72:- Minimal derived-view records or responses over turns\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:73:- Provenance from derived turns/views back to archive entries\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:86:- Treating chunks, summaries, or turns as canonical process truth\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:109:links needed for later turn derivation.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:155:  - Then: The platform returns them in a stable deterministic order\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:220:4. User reloads or returns later\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:240:  - When: User reloads or returns to the process later\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:253:- **TC-3.3b: Missing process archive read returns not found**\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:256:  - Then: The platform returns a process-not-found error\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:268:return turns without making turns canonical truth.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:277:3. User or process reads the derived turns\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:283:**AC-4.1:** The platform can derive turns from archived entries.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-der