ses/{processId}/archive/derived-views/refresh` | Requests rebuild or refresh of derived views from canonical turns |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:523:| archiveEntryIds | array of string | yes | non-empty for non-empty turns | Archive entries grouped into this turn |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:533:| turns | array of Derived Turn | yes | present | Turns derived from archive entries |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:535:| page.nextCursor | string | no | non-empty when present | Cursor for the next page when more turns exist |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:536:| page.hasMore | boolean | yes | true or false | Whether more turns are available |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:544:| viewKind | enum | yes | `turn_range` or `chunk_candidate` | Kind of structural derived view in this first slice |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:551:| viewStatus | enum | yes | `ready` or `degraded` | Whether the derived view resolved cleanly |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:552:| degradationReason | string | no | non-empty when present | Why the derived view degraded |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:559:| views | array of Derived Archive View | yes | present | Derived views over turns |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:604:- Derived-view refresh returns an accepted or settled response within 10 seconds\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:622:- One degraded archive entry, turn, or derived view does not hide healthy\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:627:- Archive append, archive read, turn derivation, derived-view refresh, and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:630:- Derived views are traceable to source turns and archive entries\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:647:4. What exact derivation rules group archive entries into turns?\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:648:5. Should turns be persisted derived records, computed on read, or cached with a\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:710:### Story 4: Turn Derivation\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:717:- AC-4.1 (turns derived from archive)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:719:- AC-4.3 (archive unchanged by turn derivation)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:724:**Delivers:** The platform exposes non-summarizing structural views over turns\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:725:with provenance back to turns and archive entries.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:729:- AC-5.1 (non-summarizing derived view over turn range)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:730:- AC-5.2 (derived view structural boundary)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:731:- AC-5.3 (derived view provenance)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:732:- AC-5.4 (derived view does not replace archive)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:737:**Delivers:** Archive entries and derived views show available artifact and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md:762:- [ ] Flows cover archive capture, finalization, read, turn derivation, derived\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/03-markdown-and-mermaid-review.md:75:This story consumes the selected artifact version from Story 2 and turns it into readable markdown with bounded render failures.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/03-markdown-and-mermaid-review.md:81:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns review data for one artifact and its versions; optional query state may select one version |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/00-foundation.md:61:| Get project shell | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project-level artifact state with project-scoped artifact identity and latest version summary |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/00-foundation.md:62:| Get process work surface | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/00-foundation.md:63:| Get review workspace | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns process-scoped review targets based on process reference and package context |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/00-foundation.md:64:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/00-foundation.md:65:| Get package review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns one package with pinned member versions even when members were produced by multiple processes |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md:86:| Get project shell | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project-level artifact state with project-scoped artifact identity and latest version summary |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md:87:| Get process work surface | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md:88:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-client.md:357:| TC-3.5b | failed submission does not create partial history | `tests/service/client/process-response-composer.test.ts` | API returns error | No misleading history item created |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:37:| TC-1.1a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-1.1a creates a project-scoped source attachment` | POST project route returns 201 summary |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:43:| TC-1.4a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-1.4a rejects invalid repository identity without partial row` | Mock resolver returns invalid; store unchanged |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:44:| TC-1.4b | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-1.4b rejects inaccessible repository without partial row` | Mock resolver returns inaccessible; 503 |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:46:| TC-2.2a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-2.2a updates source metadata` | PATCH route returns updated summary |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:54:| TC-3.3a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.3a refresh updates one source in place` | Response returns settled source summary |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:56:| TC-4.1a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-4.1a returns informing source provenance` | GET process provenance includes `informed_work` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:58:| TC-4.2a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-4.2a returns receiving source provenance` | GET process provenance includes `received_code_update` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:62:| TC-5.1a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | `TC-5.1a detaches project-scoped source` | DELETE returns detached response |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:67:| TC-6.1a | `tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.1a reopens project source attachment state` | GET project shell returns source state after reload |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:68:| TC-6.1b | `tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.1b reopens process source attachment state` | GET process work surface returns current sources |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:71:| TC-6.3a | `tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.3a one failing source does not hide healthy sources` | Section returns healthy rows plus bounded error/degraded row |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:54:| Epic 5's error-response table does not distinguish between review-workspace bootstrap reads, which benefit from bounded degraded target states, and target-specific follow-up reads, which can legitimately return request-level 404/409 responses | Data Contracts → Error Responses; AC-5.3, AC-5.4 | Design keeps the existing review-workspace bootstrap pattern: once project/process context resolves, `GET /review` returns `200` with bounded `target.status` / `target.error` degradation. Target-specific follow-up reads continue to use request-level `404` / `409` when the caller asks for an explicit missing version, missing member, or disallowed publication member | Resolved — clarified |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:30:only, leaves archive and derived views to Epic 7, and defers MCP/external-source\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:36:| Refresh cannot always settle synchronously | AC-3.3, Refresh Response | Design returns `refreshStatus: settled | pending | failed`, with pending as operation metadata rather than a fifth hydration state. | Resolved - clarified |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:52:| 4 | What exact refresh/freshness policy maps to the four source states? | The canonical states remain `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Target-ref changes make hydrated rows stale. Refresh returns settled/pending/failed operation metadata; pending is not a fifth hydration state. Branch freshness is checked when the surface reads or refresh is requested, not by background polling. |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:675:enrichment lookup fails, the reader returns durable source identity with\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:5:Expose non-summarizing structural derived views over turns with stable boundaries and provenance back to source turns and archive entries.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:12:- **Context:** The user is running or reviewing a process after source attachments, artifact versions, and source provenance have been established. The user needs to return later, inspect what happened, and trust that derived turns or chunks did not replace the original process record.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:18:Create the first derived-view layer over turns so later chunking, retrieval, summarization, and fidelity-gradient work can build from stable structural projections without replacing archive truth.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:44:- Story 4 turn derivation\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:52:**AC-5.1:** The platform can expose a non-summarizing structural derived view over one or more turns.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:55:  - Given: A process has derived turns\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:56:  - When: User requests a derived view\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:57:  - Then: The platform returns a derived view that identifies the turn boundary and does not require generated summary text\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns.md:59:**AC-5.2:** Derived views identify structural boundaries for the turns they cover.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07-