ection.test.ts`: turn surface renders stable turn boundaries and degraded turn metadata\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:164:- Stable `turnId` is the handoff seam between turn derivation and later derived-view stories.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:168:- Prove grouping and rebuild behavior through actual turn-derivation service logic and durable projections, not by hard-coding expected turns in fixtures without exercising the derivation path.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:184:- Turn derivation returns deterministic turns from ordered archive entries\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:187:- Deriving or rebuilding turns leaves canonical archive entries unchanged\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:188:- One degraded turn does not hide other turns\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/04-turn-derivation.md:189:- Stable turn ids survive rebuilds so derived views can reference them later\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:12:- **Context:** The user is running or reviewing a process after source attachments, artifact versions, and source provenance have been established. The user needs to return later, inspect what happened, and trust that derived turns or chunks did not replace the original process record.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/07-reopen-and-degraded-archive-state.md:18:Harden the completed archive/turn/derived-view surfaces so users can return later, read durable archive truth, rebuild derived views when possible, and receive bounded pages and degraded states instead of losing the archive.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/sto