ble', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:618:  it('TC-3.2b returns REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND when the process neither references nor pins the artifact', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:696:  it('TC-2.3b returns artifact versions newest to oldest', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:727:  it('TC-2.4a returns the no-version empty state for an owned artifact with no durable revisions', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:764:  it('TC-3.4c returns ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND when an explicit version is requested for a zero-version artifact', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts:796:  it('returns a ready empty markdown review when a durable version body is zero-byte', async () => {\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/test-plan.md:223:| TC-3.4b | direct zero-version artifact review returns bounded empty state | Empty, not unavailable |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/test-plan.md:224:| TC-3.4c | explicit version request against zero-version artifact returns `ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND` | Exact request-level classification |\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:550:  it('returns PROCESS_ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE when start is attempted outside the draft state', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:570:  it('returns PROCESS_ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE when resume is attempted outside the paused or interrupted states', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:590:  it('returns PROCESS_ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE when respond is attempted outside a waiting state', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:907:  it('S2-TC-2.1a: start returns environment.state = preparing in the same session', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:971:  it('S2-TC-2.1b: resume returns environment.state = preparing when environment work is required', async () => {\\\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/code-checkpoint-writer.ts:10: * is not writable, the writer returns `outcome: 'failed'` with a meaningful\\\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/code-checkpoint-writer.ts:122:   * records calls and returns canned responses. Production omits this and the\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:253:  - When: User returns from review\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:254:  - Then: The user returns to that same process context\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:474:4. System returns export metadata for the reviewed package\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:494:  - Then: The platform returns a markdown package (`.mpkz`) export for that currently reviewed package\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:535:2. User reloads, leaves and returns later, or encounters unavailable review\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:629:Export is a two-phase flow. The POST endpoint returns export metadata including a signed download URL with a bounded expiry; the browser then follows that URL to a GET endpoint that streams the archive bytes.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:633:| Get process review workspace | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns the current review workspace bootstrap for one process |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:634:| Get artifact review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns review data for one artifact and its versions; optional query state may select one version |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:635:| Get package review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns review data for one output package; optional query state may select one member |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:636:| Request package export | POST | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}/export` | Phase 1 of export. Validates exportability, mints a signed download URL with bounded expiry, returns an `ExportPackageResponse` including `downloadUrl` and `expiresAt` |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:637:| Download package export | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/exports/{exportId}` | Phase 2 of export. Consumes the signed token issued by the POST, re-verifies access and exportability, and streams the `.mpkz` archive as `application/gzip`. Returns `404 REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` when the token is expired, tampered, or missing |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:773:member that cannot be reviewed still returns identity and an explanation\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/epic.md:844:returns `target.status: unavailable` with `error.code:\\\\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:138:  it('TC-3.1a returns populated shell section envelopes sorted by updatedAt descending', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:373:  it('TC-6.3a returns an artifact section error without blocking healthy sections', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:415:  it('returns project artifact summaries without legacy process ownership fields', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:568:  it('TC-6.3b returns a source section error without blocking healthy sections', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:610:  it('TC-6.3c returns a process section error without blocking healthy sections', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts:689:  it('TC-6.2a returns 404 without leaking removed project data', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/script-execution.service.test.ts:76:  it(\\\\\\\"returns the provider's ExecutionResult unchanged\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/daytona-provider-adapter.test.ts:163:  it('creates a sandbox and returns its id/workspace handle from ensureEnvironment', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:262:  it('TC-1.1a bootstrap returns environment state on first load', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:324:  it('TC-1.1b bootstrap returns explicit absent environment state for an early process', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:370:  it('TC-1.1g bootstrap returns stale environment truth from durable state', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:433:  it('bootstrap returns latest checkpoint visibility when one exists', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:1509:  it('returns stable section error envelopes without collapsing the whole surface', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:1580:  it('returns environment unavailable instead of collapsing the whole surface when the environment read fails', async () => {\\\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter-registry.ts:38: * Test-only registry that returns the same adapter for every `providerKind`.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-server.md:229:  member set exactly, the mutation returns the existing row without creating a\\\\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:8:  it('NullPlatformStore returns false because it has no durable recovery materials', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:16:  it('returns false when no materials, no outputs, and no sources are seeded', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:24:  it('returns false when seeded with empty arrays for refs and outputs', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:42:  it('returns true when at least one current artifact id exists', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:57:  it('returns true when at least one source attachment id exists', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/platform-store-recovery-materials.test.ts:72:  it('returns true when at least one process output exists (no artifact refs)', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/nfr.test.ts:287:  it('returns a 20-member package review within 2 seconds', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/code-checkpoint-writer.test.ts:25:  it('FailingCodeCheckpointWriter returns a failed outcome with failureReason', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-html-routes.test.ts:115:  it('TC-6.4a missing process route returns a process unavailable shell', async () => {\\\\n./tests/fixtures/archive.ts:244:  bodyText: 'Potential packing window for turns 0-1.',\\\\n./tests/fixtures/archive.ts:274:  turns: [readyArchiveTurnFixture, degradedArchiveTurnFixture],\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:270:  - Then: The system returns a bounded unavailable result\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:286:list, but direct review access returns a bounded empty review state instead of\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:293:- **TC-3.4b: Zero-version direct review path returns empty state**\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:302:  - Then: The system returns `ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND` rather than the\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:405:1. User returns later to a process work surface or review workspace\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:420:  - When: The user returns later to a process that still references that\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:425:  - When: The user returns later to review that package\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:485:| Get project shell | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project-level artifact state with project-scoped artifact identity and latest version summary |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:486:| Get process work surface | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:487:| Get review workspace | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns process-scoped review targets based on process reference and package context |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:488:| Get artifact review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:489:| Get package review target | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns one package with pinned member versions even when members were produced by multiple processes |\\\\n./tests/service/server/review-workspace-api.test.ts:239:  it('TC-1.1e direct review route with zero targets returns the empty target state payload', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/project-create-api.test.ts:33:  it('TC-2.1a creates a project, assigns the owner, and returns an empty shell response', async () => {\\\\n./tests/service/server/process-environment-fire-and-forget.test.ts:78:  // turns. Polling with a small sleep keeps the test stable.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states.md:131:context, the bootstrap stays `200` and returns `target.status: unavailable`\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:63:The platform does not replace those inputs. It turns them into a coherent\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:276:and other managed views are later derived projections over turns.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:371:The user leaves and returns later. The project shell must restore enough state\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:375:returns, the system restores the project, current processes, current artifact\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:682:**AC-31:** When the user returns after leaving a project, published process\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:749:**AC-42:** The platform can derive turns from archived entries and later produce\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:750:chunks, summaries, and other managed views from those turns without mutating\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:780:  derived views over turns.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/01-review-entry-and-workspace-bootstrap.md:98:  - When: User returns from review\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/01-review-entry-and-workspace-bootstrap.md:99:  - Then: The user returns to that same process context\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:36:| Export response contract has `downloadUrl` and `expiresAt` fields that imply a two-phase export flow, but initial server-side Flow 5 design described a single-phase inline streaming response | Data Contracts → Export Package Response; AC-5 | **Two-phase flow.** POST `/api/.../packages/:packageId/export` returns 200 JSON `ExportPackageResponse` with a signed GET URL. Client renders a download link; user-initiated GET streams the `.mpkz` bytes. Expired URL retrieval returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`, matching TC-5.3b. | Resolved — clarified |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:71:Epic 4 is the first slice of Liminal Build's review layer. Epic 1 established the project shell, Epic 2 the process work surface, and Epic 3 the environment lifecycle and durable checkpointing that turns process-local work into canonical artifact state. What Epic 3 ends with is a process that can produce durable artifact outputs and code-change records — but those outputs are only visible as current-state projections on the process surface. You cannot yet open an artifact, read its body, compare it to a prior version, or bundle a set of artifacts as a reviewable output package. Epic 4 fills exactly that gap.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:81:The review surface itself is intentionally simpler than the process work surface: no live updates, no websocket subscription, no same-session reconciliation. A durable bootstrap returns the review workspace state, reopen restores durable state, and one failing review target degrades to a bounded failure envelope without taking down the rest of the surface. That simpler contract means the client work is significantly lighter than the process surface — no second live transport, no complex reconnect/sequence logic — which in turn makes room for the genuinely new surface concerns: markdown rendering, Mermaid hydration, version switching, and package navigation.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:161:`pnpm audit` remains broken in this repo because the underlying npm audit endpoint returns 410, and `npm audit` is not a valid substitute without a `package-lock.json`. Epic 3's tech design already flagged this; Epic 4 inherits the same limitation. Direct-dependency pressure testing via manual registry + advisory DB lookups is the current ceiling. A pnpm-compatible transitive-audit workflow should land before environment/runtime dependency work is treated as fully validated — tracked in Deferred Items alongside Epic 3's note.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:198:On the server, `markdown-it@14.1.1` is configured with `html: false` (stricter than MDV — we ingest agentic output, not user-authored files), extended with `@shikijs/markdown-it` (Shiki syntax highlighting), the vendored `markdown-it-anchor` (with the vendored `github-slugger`), and the purpose-built task-list renderer. Mermaid fences are intercepted: the server strips `%%{init}%%`, `%%{config}%%`, and `%%{wrap}%%` directives from each Mermaid source (closing the LobeChat/Docmost/OneUptime CVE class), then emits a placeholder div (`<div class=\\\\\\\"mermaid-placeholder\\\\\\\" data-block-id=\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\"></div>`) into the rendered HTML and returns the sanitized Mermaid source as a sidecar entry in the `mermaidBlocks` array on the response. `isomorphic-dompurify@3.9.0` post-processes the rendered HTML with `USE_PROFILES: { html: true }` plus `FORBID_TAGS: ['style', 'math', 'form']`, `FORBID_ATTR: ['style']`, `ALLOW_DATA_ATTR: false`, `ALLOW_ARIA_ATTR: false`, and a narrow `ADD_ATTR: ['data-block-id']` allowlist for the Mermaid placeholder. SVG does not appear in the server-rendered HTML (Mermaid SVG is generated and sanitized client-side).\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:222:The failure boundary sits one level below the review workspace envelope. Request-level errors (401, 403, 404, 503) apply only to resolution and authorization — the response cannot be produced at all. Once project identity, process identity, and target identity resolve, the response always returns 200 with the review workspace envelope populated. Problems *inside* that envelope surface as bounded degraded states on specific fields:\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:286:| Review workspace bootstrap API | `GET /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review` | Returns project + process + availableTargets + optional target for the selected review target |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:287:| Artifact review target API | `GET /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review/artifacts/:artifactId` | Returns one artifact's version list, selected version detail, and Mermaid sidecar |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:288:| Package review target API | `GET /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review/packages/:packageId` | Returns one package snapshot with members and the selected member's artifact detail |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:289:| Export package action | `POST /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review/packages/:packageId/export` | Phase 1 of export: returns signed download metadata for a `.mpkz` archive; the subsequent GET to `/review/exports/:exportId` performs the actual byte stream |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:299:| File content retrieval via Convex File Storage URL | Fastify obtains a Convex-issued URL via `ctx.storage.getUrl()` and fetches content once per render — **the URL never leaves the Fastify process**. `ctx.storage.getUrl()` returns a URL whose storage ID is the sole credential (verified against Convex docs + maintainer guidance in get-convex/convex-backend#328 on 2026-04-17): the URL is fully public, does not expire, cannot be revoked short of blob deletion, and anyone who obtains it can fetch the content. Fastify therefore acts as an auth-proxy: it reads with the storage URL internally and streams bytes through its own authenticated route. Storage URLs are **never** returned in HTTP response bodies, never written to structured logs, never included in error payloads, and never visible to browser code |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:399:│   │   ├── export.service.ts                      # two-phase: POST returns signed URL JSON; GET streams bytes\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:528:| Chunk 5 | Package export (two-phase): streaming `createPackageFromEntries` in the workspace package; tar hardening (gzip-bomb cap, per-entry + cumulative byte caps, entry-name filter); Fastify POST export (returns signed-URL JSON) + GET download (streams bytes); signed URL mint + verify; expired-URL 404; unsupported-but-durable members remain exportable while unavailable members block export; `mdvpkg` CLI polish | AC-5.1 through AC-5.3 | export service, export-url-signing, `@liminal-build/markdown-package/tar/create-from-entries.ts`, export trigger UI |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:555:- **Export flow is two-phase**: POST `/api/.../packages/:packageId/export` returns 200 JSON with a signed GET URL and `expiresAt`. User's browser GETs the signed URL to stream the `.mpkz` bytes. Expired URL retrieval returns 404 `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`. Matches the epic's `ExportPackageResponse` contract and TC-5.3b cleanly.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:560:- **Bootstrap error taxonomy**: review-workspace bootstrap returns a bounded `200` unavailable target state when project/process context resolves but the selected target no longer resolves in that context. Request-level `404 REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` remains for target-specific endpoints and expired/tampered export-download URLs.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:36:history at low-level entry grain, from which turns, chunks, summaries, and\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:84:| Archive | Fastify + Convex + cache/index layers | Full-fidelity low-level process history, turn derivation, later chunk/view derivation inputs | Processes | Canonical history is preserved at entry grain; turns and chunks are derived over it |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:171:| Full-fidelity archive entries are canonical while turns are derived | Context-management features can evolve without rewriting the archive |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:172:| Chunks summarize turns instead of replacing them | Derived views remain rebuildable from the archive |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:336:`Chunk` is a later derived grouping over one or more turns.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:342:**Consequence:** Archive entries carry the information needed to derive turns.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:576:  already-grouped turns or already-compressed summaries as canonical history.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/04-package-review-workspace.md:101:| Get package review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns review data for one output package; optional query state may select one member |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:6:- Current Story: 04-turn-derivation\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:33:- 04-turn-derivation\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:34:- 05-minimal-structural-views-over-turns\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:185:- Story 4 owns deterministic turn derivation and cached rebuildable turn projections without mutating archive entries.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/team-impl-log.md:186:- Story 5 owns non-summarizing structural derived views over turns, list/refresh routes, provenance to turns/archive entries, degraded/conflict behavior, and client rendering.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:27:- Zero-version direct review returns bounded empty state\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:66:  - Then: The system returns a bounded unavailable result\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:79:**AC-3.4:** Zero-version artifacts are excluded from the default review target list, but direct review access returns a bounded empty review state instead of an unavailable error.\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:85:- **TC-3.4b: Zero-version direct review path returns empty state**\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:92:  - Then: The system returns `ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND` rather than the bounded empty zero-version state\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:102:| Get review workspace | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns process-scoped review targets based on process reference and package context |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/03-process-scoped-artifact-review-realignment.md:103:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:62:| Get process review workspace | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review` | Returns the current review workspace bootstrap for one process |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:63:| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns review data for one artifact and its versions |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:64:| Get package review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}` | Returns review data for one output package and its members |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:66:| Request package export | `POST` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/packages/{packageId}/export` | Validates exportability and returns signed download metadata for one reviewed package |\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/05-reopen-and-degraded-provenance-states.md:51:  - When: The user returns later to a process that still references that artifact\\\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifa