\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_0\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"todo_list\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"items\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Read required verification docs and Convex guidelines, extracting AC/TC expectations\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Inspect implementation and tests for Story 2 production paths and archive boundary behavior\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Run required verification gates and synthesize evidence-backed findings into the JSON payload\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\":false}]}}\\\\n4:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -l docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n5:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n6:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -l docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"     176 docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md\\\\\\\\n     726 docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\\\\\\\\n     149 docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\\\\\\\\n    1051 total\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n7:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Convex guidelines\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Function guidelines\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Http endpoint syntax\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- HTTP endpoints are defined in `convex/http.ts` and require an `httpAction` decorator. For example:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```typescript\\\\\\\\nimport { httpRouter } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex/server\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { httpAction } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"./_generated/server\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nconst http = httpRouter();\\\\\\\\nhttp.route({\\\\\\\\n  path: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/echo\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  method: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"POST\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  handler: httpAction(async (ctx, req) => {\\\\\\\\n    const body = await req.bytes();\\\\\\\\n    return new Response(body, { status: 200 });\\\\\\\\n  }),\\\\\\\\n});\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- HTTP endpoints are always registered at the exact path you specify in the `path` field. For example, if you specify `/api/someRoute`, the endpoint will be registered at `/api/someRoute`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Validators\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Below is an example of an array validator:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```typescript\\\\\\\\nimport { mutation } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"./_generated/server\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { v } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex/values\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nexport default mutation({\\\\\\\\n  args: {\\\\\\\\n    simpleArray: v.array(v.union(v.string(), v.number())),\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\\\\\\\\n    //...\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n});\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Below is an example of a schema with validators that codify a discriminated union type:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```typescript\\\\\\\\nimport { defineSchema, defineTable } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex/server\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { v } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex/values\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nexport default defineSchema({\\\\\\\\n  results: defineTable(\\\\\\\\n    v.union(\\\\\\\\n      v.object({\\\\\\\\n        kind: v.literal(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"),\\\\\\\\n        errorMessage: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n      }),\\\\\\\\n      v.object({\\\\\\\\n        kind: v.literal(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"),\\\\\\\\n        value: v.number(),\\\\\\\\n      }),\\\\\\\\n    ),\\\\\\\\n  ),\\\\\\\\n});\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Here are the valid Convex types along with their respective validators:\\\\\\\\n  Convex Type | TS/JS type | Example Usage | Validator for argument validation and schemas | Notes |\\\\\\\\n  | ----------- | ------------| -----------------------| -----------------------------------------------| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\\\\\\\n  | Id | string | `doc._id` | `v.id(tableName)` | |\\\\\\\\n  | Null | null | `null` | `v.null()` | JavaScript's `undefined` is not a valid Convex value. Functions the return `undefined` or do not return will return `null` when called from a client. Use `null` instead. |\\\\\\\\n  | Int64 | bigint | `3n` | `v.int64()` | Int64s only support BigInts between -2^63 and 2^63-1. Convex supports `bigint`s in most modern browsers. |\\\\\\\\n  | Float64 | number | `3.1` | `v.number()` | Convex supports all IEEE-754 double-precision floating point numbers (such as NaNs). Inf and NaN are JSON serialized as strings. |\\\\\\\\n  | Boolean | boolean | `true` | `v.boolean()` |\\\\\\\\n  | String | string | `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` | `v.string()` | Strings are stored as UTF-8 and must be valid Unicode sequences. Strings must be smaller than the 1MB total size limit when encoded as UTF-8. |\\\\\\\\n  | Bytes | ArrayBuffer | `new ArrayBuffer(8)` | `v.bytes()` | Convex supports first class bytestrings, passed in as `ArrayBuffer`s. Bytestrings must be smaller than the 1MB total size limit for Convex types. |\\\\\\\\n  | Array | Array | `[1, 3.2, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]` | `v.array(values)` | Arrays can have at most 8192 values. |\\\\\\\\n  | Object | Object | `{a: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}` | `v.object({property: value})` | Convex only supports \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"plain old JavaScript objects\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (objects that do not have a custom prototype). Objects can have at most 1024 entries. Field names must be nonempty and not start with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". |\\\\\\\\n| Record      | Record      | `{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}` | `v.record(keys, values)`                       | Records are objects at runtime, but can have dynamic keys. Keys must be only ASCII characters, nonempty, and not start with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Function registration\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Use `internalQuery`, `internalMutation`, and `internalAction` to register internal functions. These functions are private and aren't part of an app's API. They can only be called by other Convex functions. These functions are always imported from `./_generated/server`.\\\\\\\\n- Use `query`, `mutation`, and `action` to register public functions. These functions are part of the public API and are exposed to the public Internet. Do NOT use `query`, `mutation`, or `action` to register sensitive internal functions that should be kept private.\\\\\\\\n- You CANNOT register a function through the `api` or `internal` objects.\\\\\\\\n- ALWAYS include argument validators for all Convex functions. This includes all of `query`, `internalQuery`, `mutation`, `internalMutation`, `action`, and `internalAction`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Function calling\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Use `ctx.runQuery` to call a query from a query, mutation, or action.\\\\\\\\n- Use `ctx.runMutation` to call a mutation from a mutation or action.\\\\\\\\n- Use `ctx.runAction` to call an action from an action.\\\\\\\\n- ONLY call an action from another action if you need to cross runtimes (e.g. from V8 to Node). Otherwise, pull out the shared code into a helper async function and call that directly instead.\\\\\\\\n- Try to use as few calls from actions to queries and mutations as possible. Queries and mutations are transactions, so splitting logic up into multiple calls introduces the risk of race conditions.\\\\\\\\n- All of these calls take in a `FunctionReference`. Do NOT try to pass the callee function directly into one of these calls.\\\\\\\\n- When using `ctx.runQuery`, `ctx.runMutation`, or `ctx.runAction` to call a function in the same file, specify a type annotation on the return value to work around TypeScript circularity limitations. For example,\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nexport const f = query({\\\\\\\\n  args: { name: v.string() },\\\\\\\\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\\\\\\\\n    return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Hello \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" + args.name;\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n});\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nexport const g = query({\\\\\\\\n  args: {},\\\\\\\\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\\\\\\\\n    const result: string = await ctx.runQuery(api.example.f, { name: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bob\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" });\\\\\\\\n    return null;\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n});\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Function references\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Use the `api` object defined by the framework in `convex/_generated/api.ts` to call public functions registered with `query`, `mutation`, or `action`.\\\\\\\\n- Use the `internal` object defined by the framework in `convex/_generated/api.ts` to call internal (or private) functions registered with `internalQuery`, `internalMutation`, or `internalAction`.\\\\\\\\n- Convex uses file-based routing, so a public function defined in `convex/example.ts` named `f` has a function reference of `api.example.f`.\\\\\\\\n- A private function defined in `convex/example.ts` named `g` has a function reference of `internal.example.g`.\\\\\\\\n- Functions can also registered within directories nested within the `convex/` folder. For example, a public function `h` defined in `convex/messages/access.ts` has a function reference of `api.messages.access.h`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Pagination\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Define pagination using the following syntax:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```ts\\\\\\\\nimport { v } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex/values\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { query, mutation } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"./_generated/server\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { paginationOptsValidator } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex/server\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nexport const listWithExtraArg = query({\\\\\\\\n  args: { paginationOpts: paginationOptsValidator, author: v.string() },\\\\\\\\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\\\\\\\\n    return await ctx.db\\\\\\\\n      .query(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n      .withIndex(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"by_author\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", (q) => q.eq(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"author\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", args.author))\\\\\\\\n      .order(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"desc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n      .paginate(args.paginationOpts);\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n});\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNote: `paginationOpts` is an object with the following properties:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- `numItems`: the maximum number of documents to return (the validator is `v.number()`)\\\\\\\\n- `cursor`: the cursor to use to fetch the next page of documents (the validator is `v.union(v.string(), v.null())`)\\\\\\\\n- A query that ends in `.paginate()` returns an object that has the following properties:\\\\\\\\n- page (contains an array of documents that you fetches)\\\\\\\\n- isDone (a boolean that represents whether or not this is the last page of documents)\\\\\\\\n- continueCursor (a string that represents the cursor to use to fetch the next page of documents)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Schema guidelines\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Always define your schema in `convex/schema.ts`.\\\\\\\\n- Always import the schema definition functions from `convex/server`.\\\\\\\\n- System fields are automatically added to all documents and are prefixed with an underscore. The two system fields that are automatically added to all documents are `_creationTime` which has the validator `v.number()` and `_id` which has the validator `v.id(tableName)`.\\\\\\\\n- Always include all index fields in the index name. For example, if an index is defined as `[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`, the index name should be \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"by_field1_and_field2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\n- Index fields must be queried in the same order they are defined. If you want to be able to query by \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" then \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and by \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"field2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" then \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"field1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", you must create separate indexes.\\\\\\\\n- Do not store unbounded lists as an array field inside a document (e.g. `v.array(v.object({...}))`). As the array grows it will hit the 1MB document size limit, and every update rewrites the entire document. Instead, create a separate table for the child items with a foreign key back to the parent.\\\\\\\\n- Separate high-churn operational data (e.g. heartbeats, online status, typing indicators) from stable profile data. Storing frequently updated fields on a shared document forces every write to contend with reads of the entire document. Instead, create a dedicated table for the high-churn data with a foreign key back to the parent record.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Authentication guidelines\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Convex supports JWT-based authentication through `convex/auth.config.ts`. ALWAYS create this file when using authentication. Without it, `ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()` will always return `null`.\\\\\\\\n- Example `convex/auth.config.ts`:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```typescript\\\\\\\\nexport default {\\\\\\\\n  providers: [\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      domain: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://your-auth-provider.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      applicationID: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n  ],\\\\\\\\n};\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe `domain` must be the issuer URL of the JWT provider. Convex fetches `{domain}/.well-known/openid-configuration` to discover the JWKS endpoint. The `applicationID` is checked against the JWT `aud` (audience) claim.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Use `ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()` to get the authenticated user's identity in any query, mutation, or action. This returns `null` if the user is not authenticated, or a `UserIdentity` object with fields like `subject`, `issuer`, `name`, `email`, etc. The `subject` field is the unique user identifier.\\\\\\\\n- In Convex `UserIdentity`, `tokenIdentifier` is guaranteed and is the canonical stable identifier for the authenticated identity. For any auth-linked database lookup or ownership check, prefer `identity.tokenIdentifier` over `identity.subject`. Do NOT use `identity.subject` alone as a global identity key.\\\\\\\\n- NEVER accept a `userId` or any user identifier as a function argument for authorization purposes. Always derive the user identity server-side via `ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()`.\\\\\\\\n- When using an external auth provider with Convex on the client, use `ConvexProviderWithAuth` instead of `ConvexProvider`:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```tsx\\\\\\\\nimport { ConvexProviderWithAuth, ConvexReactClient } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"convex/react\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nconst convex = new ConvexReactClient(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL!);\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nfunction App({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\\\\\\\\n  return (\\\\\\\\n    <ConvexProviderWithAuth client={convex} useAuth={useYourAuthHook}>\\\\\\\\n      {children}\\\\\\\\n    </ConvexProviderWithAuth>\\\\\\\\n  );\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe `useAuth` prop must return `{ isLoading, isAuthenticated, fetchAccessToken }`. Do NOT use plain `ConvexProvider` when authentication is needed — it will not send tokens with requests.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Typescript guidelines\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- You can use the helper typescript type `Id` imported from './\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_generated/dataModel' to get the type of the id for a given table. For example if there is a table called 'users' you can use `Id<'users'>` to get the type of the id for that table.\\\\\\\\n- Use `Doc<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tableName\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\">` from `./_generated/dataModel` to get the full document type for a table.\\\\\\\\n- Use `QueryCtx`, `MutationCtx`, `ActionCtx` from `./_generated/server` for typing function contexts. NEVER use `any` for ctx parameters — always use the proper context type.\\\\\\\\n- If you need to define a `Record` make sure that you correctly provide the type of the key and value in the type. For example a validator `v.record(v.id('users'), v.string())` would have the type `Record<Id<'users'>, string>`. Below is an example of using `Record` with an `Id` type in a query:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n```ts\\\\\\\\nimport { query } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"./_generated/server\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { Doc, Id } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"./_generated/dataModel\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nexport const exampleQuery = query({\\\\\\\\n  args: { userIds: v.array(v.id(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")) },\\\\\\\\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\\\\\\\\n    const idToUsername: Record<Id<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\">, string> = {};\\\\\\\\n    for (const userId of args.userIds) {\\\\\\\\n      const user = await ctx.db.get(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", userId);\\\\\\\\n      if (user) {\\\\\\\\n        idToUsername[user._id] = user.username;\\\\\\\\n      }\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n8:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md | sed -n '1,220p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n9:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md | sed -n '1,220p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"     1\\\\\\\\t# Story 2: Finalization Boundary Between Live State and Archive\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\t### Summary\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\tArchive completed process objects exactly once while keeping raw live streaming deltas and interrupted partial objects out of canonical archive truth.\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\t### Description\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\t**User Profile**\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\t- **Primary User:** A technical founder, tech lead, staff engineer, or agentic operator who needs process history to remain durable, inspectable, and usable for later long-horizon context management.\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\t- **Context:** The user is running or reviewing a process after source attachments, artifact versions, and source provenance have been established. The user needs to return later, inspect what happened, and trust that derived turns or chunks did not replace the original process record.\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\t- **Mental Model:** \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The platform keeps the full record of what happened. Turns, chunks, and summaries are views over that record, not the record itself.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\t- **Key Constraint:** The archive must preserve finalized low-level entries as canonical truth. It must not store raw streaming deltas, interrupted partial objects, or only pre-summarized history as the durable record.\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t**Objective**\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\tAdd the finalization service and completion-point hooks that convert finalized process objects into archive entries without changing the existing live WebSocket/current-object model.\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\t**Scope**\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\tIn:\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\t- `ArchiveFinalizationService`\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\t- Finalized object to archive-entry mapping\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\t- Accepted user response finalization\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\t- Completed model/runtime object finalization\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\t- Finalized script emission, tool call, tool result, and process event mapping where completion points exist\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\t- Excluding raw streaming deltas from archive append\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\t- Excluding interrupted partial model/tool objects from archive append\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\t- Idempotent retry behavior using `finalizationKey`\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\t- Compatibility mapping from current process history items when a finalized compatible item is explicitly bridged\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\tOut:\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\t- Replacing existing live WebSocket/upsert transport\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\t- Publishing archive entries back into live history\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\t- User-visible archive route/UI work\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\t- Historical migration/backfill\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\t- Process-specific summarization or context packing\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\t**Dependencies**\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\t- Story 1 canonical archive entry persistence\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\t- Existing process response/action services and live normalizer\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\t- Existing process history presentation surface\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\t- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md)\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\t- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md)\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\t**AC-2.1:** Raw streaming deltas are not stored as canonical archive entries.\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t- **TC-2.1a: Streaming delta excluded from archive**\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\t  - Given: A live model or runtime stream emits partial deltas\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\t  - When: The process archive is read\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\t  - Then: Raw deltas do not appear as archive entries\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\t**AC-2.2:** Interrupted partial objects are not archived as finalized entries.\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\t- **TC-2.2a: Interrupted model output excluded**\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\t  - Given: A model output begins but is interrupted before finalization\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\t  - When: The process archive is read\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\t  - Then: The interrupted partial object is not returned as a finalized archive entry\\\\\\\\n    65\\\\\\\\t- **TC-2.2b: Interrupted tool result excluded**\\\\\\\\n    66\\\\\\\\t  - Given: A tool call begins but never receives a finalized result\\\\\\\\n    67\\\\\\\\t  - When: The process archive is read\\\\\\\\n    68\\\\\\\\t  - Then: The incomplete tool result is not returned as a finalized archive entry\\\\\\\\n    69\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    70\\\\\\\\t**AC-2.3:** Finalization services append completed live objects into the canonical archive exactly once.\\\\\\\\n    71\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    72\\\\\\\\t- **TC-2.3a: Completed live object archived once through finalization service**\\\\\\\\n    73\\\\\\\\t  - Given: The browser received live upserts for an in-flight object\\\\\\\\n    74\\\\\\\\t  - When: The object completes\\\\\\\\n    75\\\\\\\\t  - Then: The platform appends one finalized archive entry for that object through the finalization service\\\\\\\\n    76\\\\\\\\t- **TC-2.3b: Replayed completion does not duplicate archive entry through service boundary**\\\\\\\\n    77\\\\\\\\t  - Given: A completion event is retried for an already-archived object\\\\\\\\n    78\\\\\\\\t  - When: The finalization service processes the retry\\\\\\\\n    79\\\\\\\\t  - Then: The platform does not create a duplicate canonical entry\\\\\\\\n    80\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    81\\\\\\\\t### Technical Design\\\\\\\\n    82\\\\\\\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\\\\\\\n    83\\\\\\\\tThis story owns the separation between active live state and canonical archive finalization.\\\\\\\\n    84\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    85\\\\\\\\t#### Architecture Context\\\\\\\\n    86\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    87\\\\\\\\tStory 2 is the control-plane finalization seam. It decides which completed\\\\\\\\n    88\\\\\\\\tprocess/runtime objects become canonical archive entries, proves those objects\\\\\\\\n    89\\\\\\\\tappend exactly once through the service boundary, and protects the existing live\\\\\\\\n    90\\\\\\\\tWebSocket/upsert model from quietly becoming archive truth.\\\\\\\\n    91\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    92\\\\\\\\t#### Service Interface\\\\\\\\n    93\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    94\\\\\\\\t| Method | Description |\\\\\\\\n    95\\\\\\\\t|---|---|\\\\\\\\n    96\\\\\\\\t| `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFinalizedEntry(args)` | Validates a completed object and appends one finalized archive entry through `PlatformStore` |\\\\\\\\n    97\\\\\\\\t| `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem(args)` | Maps a finalized compatible current-history item to one archive entry or returns `null` when no safe mapping exists |\\\\\\\\n    98\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    99\\\\\\\\t#### Finalization Keys\\\\\\\\n   100\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   101\\\\\\\\t| Finalized Object | Example `finalizationKey` |\\\\\\\\n   102\\\\\\\\t|---|---|\\\\\\\\n   103\\\\\\\\t| Accepted user response | `response:{clientRequestId}` |\\\\\\\\n   104\\\\\\\\t| Runtime model message | `model:{sourceObjectId}` |\\\\\\\\n   105\\\\\\\\t| Tool call | `tool:{relatedToolCallId}:call` |\\\\\\\\n   106\\\\\\\\t| Tool result | `tool:{relatedToolCallId}:result` |\\\\\\\\n   107\\\\\\\\t| Process event | `event:{sourceObjectId}` |\\\\\\\\n   108\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   109\\\\\\\\t#### Implementation Targets\\\\\\\\n   110\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   111\\\\\\\\t| Area | Files / Modules |\\\\\\\\n   112\\\\\\\\t|------|-----------------|\\\\\\\\n   113\\\\\\\\t| Finalization service | `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts` |\\\\\\\\n   114\\\\\\\\t| Process response and environment hooks | `apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts`, `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts` |\\\\\\\\n   115\\\\\\\\t| Live/archive separation | `apps/platform/server/services/processes/live/process-live-normalizer.ts`, `apps/platform/client/app/process-live.ts` |\\\\\\\\n   116\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   117\\\\\\\\tImplementation notes:\\\\\\\\n   118\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   119\\\\\\\\t- Existing live upserts remain current-object transport and do not become archive writes.\\\\\\\\n   120\\\\\\\\t- Only trusted Fastify completion points call `ArchiveFinalizationService`.\\\\\\\\n   121\\\\\\\\t- Story 1 proves primitive idempotency; this story proves completion hooks call that primitive exactly once for finalized objects.\\\\\\\\n   122\\\\\\\\t- Raw deltas, partial buffers, interrupted objects, and abandoned tool results do not call append.\\\\\\\\n   123\\\\\\\\t- Replayed completion events rely on Story 1 `finalizationKey` idempotency and must prove exactly-once archive append behavior at the service boundary.\\\\\\\\n   124\\\\\\\\t- Compatibility mapping may map finalized `process_message` to `model_message`; it must not treat arbitrary legacy presentation rows as canonical archive truth.\\\\\\\\n   125\\\\\\\\t- `process-live-normalizer.ts` remains unchanged except where tests assert live/archive separation.\\\\\\\\n   126\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   127\\\\\\\\t#### Design References\\\\\\\\n   128\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   129\\\\\\\\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:444), lines 444-505\\\\\\\\n   130\\\\\\\\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:587), lines 587-601\\\\\\\\n   131\\\\\\\\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:706), lines 706-712\\\\\\\\n   132\\\\\\\\t- [test-plan.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:45), lines 45-49\\\\\\\\n   133\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   134\\\\\\\\t#### Test Mapping\\\\\\\\n   135\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   136\\\\\\\\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\\\\\\\n   137\\\\\\\\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\\\\\\\\n   138\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.1a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | raw streaming delta excluded from archive |\\\\\\\\n   139\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.2a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | interrupted model output excluded |\\\\\\\\n   140\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.2b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | incomplete tool result excluded |\\\\\\\\n   141\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | completed live object archived once through finalization service |\\\\\\\\n   142\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | replayed completion does not duplicate entry through service boundary |\\\\\\\\n   143\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   144\\\\\\\\t#### Non-TC Decided Tests\\\\\\\\n   145\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   146\\\\\\\\t- `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts`: live history upserts still update current process history without creating archive rows\\\\\\\\n   147\\\\\\\\t- `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`: compatibility mapping from `processHistoryItems` only maps finalized compatible items\\\\\\\\n   148\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   149\\\\\\\\t#### Technical Notes\\\\\\\\n   150\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   151\\\\\\\\t- Finalization is a control-plane decision. Live upserts remain current-object transport only, and this story owns the service-level proof that finalized objects append into the archive exactly once.\\\\\\\\n   152\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   153\\\\\\\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\\\\\\\n   154\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   155\\\\\\\\t- Prove separation through the real append boundary; do not accept a fake implementation that merely “marks” deltas as ignored without protecting the append path.\\\\\\\\n   156\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   157\\\\\\\\t#### Verification\\\\\\\\n   158\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   159\\\\\\\\t- Targeted: `pnpm run test:service`\\\\\\\\n   160\\\\\\\\t- Story gate: `pnpm run green-verify`\\\\\\\\n   161\\\\\\\\t- Epic gate: `pnpm run verify-all`\\\\\\\\n   162\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   163\\\\\\\\t#### Spec Deviations\\\\\\\\n   164\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   165\\\\\\\\tNone.\\\\\\\\n   166\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   167\\\\\\\\tSee the tech design document for full architecture, implementation targets, and test mapping.\\\\\\\\n   168\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   169\\\\\\\\t### Definition of Done\\\\\\\\n   170\\\\\\\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\\\\\\\n   171\\\\\\\\t- `ArchiveFinalizationService` exists and maps completed objects into canonical archive entry shape\\\\\\\\n   172\\\\\\\\t- Accepted user responses, completed model messages, completed tool/script/runtime objects, and process events have defined finalization paths where those completion points exist\\\\\\\\n   173\\\\\\\\t- Raw streaming deltas and interrupted partial objects cannot append finalized archive entries\\\\\\\\n   174\\\\\\\\t- Retried completion events do not duplicate archive rows\\\\\\\\n   175\\\\\\\\t- Existing live process upserts continue to update current browser state without creating archive rows by themselves\\\\\\\\n   176\\\\\\\\t- Tests cover TC-2.1a through TC-2.3b plus live/archive separation and compatibility mapping from the test plan\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n10:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '1,500p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n11:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '1,500p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"     1\\\\\\\\t# Technical Design: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\t## Purpose\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\tThis document translates Epic 7 into an implementable design for canonical\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\tprocess archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\tIt is the implementation blueprint for preserving finalized low-level process\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\thistory while keeping live process state, turns, and derived views separate from\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\tcanonical truth.\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\t| Audience | Value |\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\t|----------|-------|\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\t| Reviewers | Validate that archive work follows the core platform architecture |\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\t| Developers | Know which routes, services, Convex functions, contracts, and tests to build |\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t| Story Tech Sections | Reuse interfaces, flow designs, TC mappings, and chunk breakdowns |\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\tRelated documents:\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\t- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\t- Architecture: `docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md`\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\t- Epic 6 tech design: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md`\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\tOutput configuration: Config A. Epic 7 gets this `tech-design.md` and a separate\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\t`test-plan.md`. The work crosses live process, Fastify, Convex, and client read\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\tsurfaces, but the archive domain is coherent enough for one index document.\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\t## Spec Validation\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\tEpic 7 is implementation-ready. It is scoped to canonical finalized archive\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\tentries, deterministic turn derivation, minimal structural derived views, and\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\tbounded degraded reads. It explicitly avoids model-generated summaries,\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\texternal-source attachment, and replacing the existing live WebSocket/upsert\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\tmodel.\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\t| Issue | Spec Location | Resolution | Status |\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\t|-------|---------------|------------|--------|\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\t| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\t| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\t| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\t| Minimal derived view could drift into summarization | AC-5.x | Design limits derived views to structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` records without generated summary body. | Resolved |\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\t| Provenance links must not duplicate Epic 5/6 ownership logic | AC-6.x | Design stores nullable related ids and enriches through existing artifact/source services at read time. Archive entries remain visible when enrichment degrades. | Resolved |\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\tNo design-time deviation from the PRD or architecture is required. Fastify owns\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\tarchive finalization policy, read orchestration, turn derivation, and derived\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\tview refresh. Convex owns durable append/read storage, ordering, idempotency\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\tguards, and optional cached projection records.\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\t## Tech Design Questions Answered\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t| # | Epic Question | Design Answer |\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\t|---|---------------|---------------|\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t| 2 | What compatibility mapping bridges `processHistoryItems` and live updates, and is migration/backfill in scope? | Add compatibility helpers that map new finalized archive entries to existing process-history surfaces where needed. Existing `processHistoryItems` remain the legacy presentation read model. No historical migration/backfill is in scope for Epic 7. |\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\t| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\t| 4 | What derivation rules group archive entries into turns? | Turn derivation is deterministic over ordered archive entries. A `user_message` starts a new turn; following model/reasoning/script/tool/process entries attach to the active turn until the next `user_message`. Tool call/result correlation keeps paired tool entries in the same turn. |\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\t| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\t| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\t| 7 | How should source/artifact provenance link without duplicating ownership logic? | Archive entries store nullable related ids (`relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, `relatedToolCallId`). Read services enrich from existing artifact/source services and degrade per entry when related records are unavailable. |\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\t| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\t| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\t## Context\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    65\\\\\\\\tThe platform already has process history, but it is presentation history. The\\\\\\\\n    66\\\\\\\\tcurrent `processHistoryItems` table supports the process work surface and live\\\\\\\\n    67\\\\\\\\thistory upserts with a smaller vocabulary: `user_message`, `process_message`,\\\\\\\\n    68\\\\\\\\t`progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and\\\\\\\\n    69\\\\\\\\t`process_event`. That is useful UI state, but it is not the full-fidelity\\\\\\\\n    70\\\\\\\\tarchive the PRD requires for long-horizon context management.\\\\\\\\n    71\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    72\\\\\\\\tEpic 7 introduces canonical archive truth without tearing out the live surface.\\\\\\\\n    73\\\\\\\\tFastify still normalizes runtime events into typed WebSocket upserts for active\\\\\\\\n    74\\\\\\\\tUI state. Separately, completed process objects are finalized into archive\\\\\\\\n    75\\\\\\\\tentries at low-level grain. This preserves the active interaction model while\\\\\\\\n    76\\\\\\\\tmaking later turn/query/chunk work rebuildable from a stable durable record.\\\\\\\\n    77\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    78\\\\\\\\tThe design is deliberately conservative around derived views. Turns and\\\\\\\\n    79\\\\\\\\tstructural views help later context-management work, but they do not replace\\\\\\\\n    80\\\\\\\\tarchive entries. A derived turn or chunk candidate can be rebuilt from the\\\\\\\\n    81\\\\\\\\tarchive. If derivation fails, the archive remains readable. That property is\\\\\\\\n    82\\\\\\\\tmore important than early summarization convenience.\\\\\\\\n    83\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    84\\\\\\\\tEpic 7 also consumes Epic 5 and Epic 6 provenance without taking ownership of\\\\\\\\n    85\\\\\\\\tthose domains. Artifact versions keep producing-process provenance in the\\\\\\\\n    86\\\\\\\\tartifact/version model. Source provenance keeps repository identity in Epic 6\\\\\\\\n    87\\\\\\\\trecords. Archive entries may link to those records and show related context, but\\\\\\\\n    88\\\\\\\\tthey do not redefine artifact ownership or source attachment lifecycle.\\\\\\\\n    89\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    90\\\\\\\\t## System View\\\\\\\\n    91\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    92\\\\\\\\t### Top-Tier Surfaces\\\\\\\\n    93\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    94\\\\\\\\t| Surface | Source | This Epic's Role |\\\\\\\\n    95\\\\\\\\t|---------|--------|------------------|\\\\\\\\n    96\\\\\\\\t| Processes | Core architecture | Finalization points and archive read access live under one project/process |\\\\\\\\n    97\\\\\\\\t| Archive | Core architecture | Primary Epic 7 domain; owns canonical entries and rebuildable projections |\\\\\\\\n    98\\\\\\\\t| Projects | Core architecture | Project/process access gates archive reads |\\\\\\\\n    99\\\\\\\\t| Artifacts | Core architecture | Provides related artifact-version context during archive reads |\\\\\\\\n   100\\\\\\\\t| Sources | Core architecture + Epic 6 | Provides related source provenance context during archive reads |\\\\\\\\n   101\\\\\\\\t| Client | Core architecture | Adds process-surface entry points for archive, turn, and structural-view reads |\\\\\\\\n   102\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   103\\\\\\\\t### Runtime Flow\\\\\\\\n   104\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   105\\\\\\\\t```mermaid\\\\\\\\n   106\\\\\\\\tflowchart LR\\\\\\\\n   107\\\\\\\\t    EXEC[Process/runtime completion points]\\\\\\\\n   108\\\\\\\\t    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\\\\\\\\n   109\\\\\\\\t    STORE[PlatformStore]\\\\\\\\n   110\\\\\\\\t    X[(Convex Archive Tables)]\\\\\\\\n   111\\\\\\\\t    READ[ArchiveReadService]\\\\\\\\n   112\\\\\\\\t    DERIVE[TurnDerivationService]\\\\\\\\n   113\\\\\\\\t    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\\\\\\\\n   114\\\\\\\\t    API[Fastify archive routes]\\\\\\\\n   115\\\\\\\\t    UI[Client process/archive UI]\\\\\\\\n   116\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   117\\\\\\\\t    EXEC --> FINAL\\\\\\\\n   118\\\\\\\\t    FINAL --> STORE\\\\\\\\n   119\\\\\\\\t    STORE --> X\\\\\\\\n   120\\\\\\\\t    UI --> API\\\\\\\\n   121\\\\\\\\t    API --> READ\\\\\\\\n   122\\\\\\\\t    READ --> STORE\\\\\\\\n   123\\\\\\\\t    READ --> DERIVE\\\\\\\\n   124\\\\\\\\t    DERIVE --> VIEWS\\\\\\\\n   125\\\\\\\\t    VIEWS --> STORE\\\\\\\\n   126\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   127\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   128\\\\\\\\tThe append path is narrow and trusted. Fastify calls\\\\\\\\n   129\\\\\\\\t`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\\\\\\\\n   130\\\\\\\\tnormalizes the finalized object into canonical archive entry shape and asks\\\\\\\\n   131\\\\\\\\t`PlatformStore` to append it. Convex assigns sequence and enforces idempotency.\\\\\\\\n   132\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   133\\\\\\\\tThe read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\\\\\\\\n   134\\\\\\\\tentries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\\\\\\\\n   135\\\\\\\\tstructural views. These services read durable archive data and enrich related\\\\\\\\n   136\\\\\\\\tartifact/source context independently. A related-context failure degrades one\\\\\\\\n   137\\\\\\\\tentry or view rather than hiding the archive.\\\\\\\\n   138\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   139\\\\\\\\t## Decisions\\\\\\\\n   140\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   141\\\\\\\\t| Decision | Rationale | Consequence |\\\\\\\\n   142\\\\\\\\t|----------|-----------|-------------|\\\\\\\\n   143\\\\\\\\t| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\\\\\\\\n   144\\\\\\\\t| Fastify owns finalization policy | Architecture says Fastify owns orchestration and live-event normalization | Convex append functions are durable primitives with validators and idempotency guards |\\\\\\\\n   145\\\\\\\\t| Convex assigns `sequence` atomically | Stable ordering must survive same timestamps and retries | Append mutation computes next sequence per process |\\\\\\\\n   146\\\\\\\\t| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\\\\\\\\n   147\\\\\\\\t| Turn references must stay stable across rebuilds | Derived views cannot dangle when turn cache is refreshed | Turns get deterministic `turnId` values and derived views store stable turn ids plus turn-index ranges, not Convex row ids |\\\\\\\\n   148\\\\\\\\t| Derived views are structural only | Prevents scope creep into summarization | `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` contain boundaries/provenance, not generated summaries |\\\\\\\\n   149\\\\\\\\t| No historical migration/backfill | Epic 7 is forward canonicalization plus compatibility bridge | Existing `processHistoryItems` remain visible, but old rows are not retroactively canonical |\\\\\\\\n   150\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   151\\\\\\\\t## Module Boundaries\\\\\\\\n   152\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   153\\\\\\\\t### File Architecture\\\\\\\\n   154\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   155\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   156\\\\\\\\tconvex/\\\\\\\\n   157\\\\\\\\t├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\\\\\\\\n   158\\\\\\\\t├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\\\\\\\\n   159\\\\\\\\t├── derivedArchiveViews.ts                    # NEW: structural derived-view records\\\\\\\\n   160\\\\\\\\t└── schema.ts                                 # MODIFIED: archive tables and indexes\\\\\\\\n   161\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   162\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/shared/contracts/\\\\\\\\n   163\\\\\\\\t├── archive.ts                                # NEW: archive/turn/derived-view contracts and route builders\\\\\\\\n   164\\\\\\\\t├── process-work-surface.ts                   # MODIFIED: optional archive entry points/actions in process surface contract\\\\\\\\n   165\\\\\\\\t└── index.ts                                  # MODIFIED: exports\\\\\\\\n   166\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   167\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/server/schemas/\\\\\\\\n   168\\\\\\\\t└── archive.ts                                # NEW: Fastify route schemas for archive APIs\\\\\\\\n   169\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   170\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/server/routes/\\\\\\\\n   171\\\\\\\\t└── archive.ts                                # NEW: authenticated archive/turn/derived-view routes\\\\\\\\n   172\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   173\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/server/services/archive/\\\\\\\\n   174\\\\\\\\t├── archive-finalization.service.ts           # NEW: finalized-object to archive-entry mapping\\\\\\\\n   175\\\\\\\\t├── archive-read.service.ts                   # NEW: archive read/enrichment/degraded-state orchestration\\\\\\\\n   176\\\\\\\\t├── turn-derivation.service.ts                # NEW: deterministic turn derivation and rebuild\\\\\\\\n   177\\\\\\\\t├── derived-archive-view.service.ts           # NEW: structural view creation/read/refresh\\\\\\\\n   178\\\\\\\\t└── process-history-compat.service.ts         # NEW: bridge archive entries to existing history surface when needed\\\\\\\\n   179\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   180\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/server/services/projects/\\\\\\\\n   181\\\\\\\\t└── platform-store.ts                         # MODIFIED: archive append/read/projection methods\\\\\\\\n   182\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   183\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/server/services/processes/\\\\\\\\n   184\\\\\\\\t├── environment/process-environment.service.ts # MODIFIED: call finalization for execution/tool/process events\\\\\\\\n   185\\\\\\\\t├── process-response.service.ts               # MODIFIED: archive accepted user responses\\\\\\\\n   186\\\\\\\\t└── live/process-live-normalizer.ts           # UNCHANGED: live upserts remain current-object transport\\\\\\\\n   187\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   188\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/client/features/processes/\\\\\\\\n   189\\\\\\\\t├── archive-section.ts                        # NEW: process archive read surface\\\\\\\\n   190\\\\\\\\t├── archive-turns-section.ts                  # NEW: derived turn surface\\\\\\\\n   191\\\\\\\\t└── derived-archive-views-section.ts          # NEW: structural derived-view surface\\\\\\\\n   192\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   193\\\\\\\\tapps/platform/client/app/\\\\\\\\n   194\\\\\\\\t└── bootstrap.ts                              # MODIFIED: route archive actions to process/archive surfaces\\\\\\\\n   195\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   196\\\\\\\\ttests/\\\\\\\\n   197\\\\\\\\t├── fixtures/archive.ts                       # NEW: archive/turn/view fixtures\\\\\\\\n   198\\\\\\\\t├── service/server/archive-api.test.ts        # NEW: Fastify archive route tests\\\\\\\\n   199\\\\\\\\t├── service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts # NEW: finalization and idempotency tests\\\\\\\\n   200\\\\\\\\t├── service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts    # NEW: deterministic turn derivation tests\\\\\\\\n   201\\\\\\\\t├── service/client/archive-section.test.ts    # NEW: client archive rendering tests\\\\\\\\n   202\\\\\\\\t├── service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts # NEW: turn surface rendering tests\\\\\\\\n   203\\\\\\\\t└── service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts # NEW: derived-view UI tests\\\\\\\\n   204\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   205\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   206\\\\\\\\t### Module Responsibility Matrix\\\\\\\\n   207\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   208\\\\\\\\t| Module | Status | Responsibility | Dependencies | ACs Covered |\\\\\\\\n   209\\\\\\\\t|--------|--------|----------------|--------------|-------------|\\\\\\\\n   210\\\\\\\\t| `convex/archiveEntries.ts` | New | Append/read canonical entries, sequence assignment, idempotency guard, pagination | Convex schema | AC-1.x, AC-2.3, AC-3.x, AC-7.3 |\\\\\\\\n   211\\\\\\\\t| `convex/archiveTurns.ts` | New | Store rebuildable cached turns | Convex schema | AC-4.x, AC-7.1 |\\\\\\\\n   212\\\\\\\\t| `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts` | New | Store/read structural derived views | Convex schema | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\\\\\\\\n   213\\\\\\\\t| `ArchiveFinalizationService` | New | Map completed process objects to archive entries; exclude deltas/partials | PlatformStore | AC-1.x, AC-2.x |\\\\\\\\n   214\\\\\\\\t| `ArchiveReadService` | New | Read archive entries, enforce access via routes/services, enrich related context, degrade locally | PlatformStore, artifact/source services | AC-3.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\\\\\\\\n   215\\\\\\\\t| `TurnDerivationService` | New | Deterministically derive/rebuild turns from archive entries | PlatformStore | AC-4.x |\\\\\\\\n   216\\\\\\\\t| `DerivedArchiveViewService` | New | Build/read non-summarizing structural views | PlatformStore, TurnDerivationService | AC-5.x, AC-7.x |\\\\\\\\n   217\\\\\\\\t| `ProcessHistoryCompatService` | New | Bridge archive entries to existing history surfaces without migration | ArchiveReadService | A7, Story 0 |\\\\\\\\n   218\\\\\\\\t| `registerArchiveRoutes` | New | Fastify entry points, auth/access, request/response validation | ProcessAccessService, archive services | AC-3.x through AC-7.x |\\\\\\\\n   219\\\\\\\\t| Client archive sections | New | Render archive, turns, structural views, empty/degraded states | Shared contracts/API client | AC-3.x, AC-4.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.x, AC-7.x |\\\\\\\\n   220\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   221\\\\\\\\t## Data Model\\\\\\\\n   222\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   223\\\\\\\\t### Convex `archiveEntries`\\\\\\\\n   224\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   225\\\\\\\\t```typescript\\\\\\\\n   226\\\\\\\\texport const archiveEntryKindValidator = v.union(\\\\\\\\n   227\\\\\\\\t  v.literal('user_message'),\\\\\\\\n   228\\\\\\\\t  v.literal('model_message'),\\\\\\\\n   229\\\\\\\\t  v.literal('reasoning'),\\\\\\\\n   230\\\\\\\\t  v.literal('script_emission'),\\\\\\\\n   231\\\\\\\\t  v.literal('tool_call'),\\\\\\\\n   232\\\\\\\\t  v.literal('tool_result'),\\\\\\\\n   233\\\\\\\\t  v.literal('process_event'),\\\\\\\\n   234\\\\\\\\t);\\\\\\\\n   235\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   236\\\\\\\\texport const archiveEntriesTableFields = {\\\\\\\\n   237\\\\\\\\t  projectId: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   238\\\\\\\\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\\\\\\\\n   239\\\\\\\\t  entryKind: archiveEntryKindValidator,\\\\\\\\n   240\\\\\\\\t  sequence: v.number(),\\\\\\\\n   241\\\\\\\\t  lifecycleState: v.literal('finalized'),\\\\\\\\n   242\\\\\\\\t  finalizationKey: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   243\\\\\\\\t  sourceObjectId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   244\\\\\\\\t  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   245\\\\\\\\t  bodyData: v.union(\\\\\\\\n   246\\\\\\\\t    v.object({\\\\\\\\n   247\\\\\\\\t      jsonText: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   248\\\\\\\\t    }),\\\\\\\\n   249\\\\\\\\t    v.null(),\\\\\\\\n   250\\\\\\\\t  ),\\\\\\\\n   251\\\\\\\\t  bodyFormat: v.union(v.literal('plain_text'), v.literal('markdown'), v.literal('structured'), v.literal('none')),\\\\\\\\n   252\\\\\\\\t  relatedArtifactVersionId: v.union(v.id('artifactVersions'), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   253\\\\\\\\t  relatedSourceProvenanceId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   254\\\\\\\\t  relatedToolCallId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   255\\\\\\\\t  entryStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\\\\\\\\n   256\\\\\\\\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   257\\\\\\\\t  recordedAt: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   258\\\\\\\\t};\\\\\\\\n   259\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   260\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   261\\\\\\\\tIndexes:\\\\\\\\n   262\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   263\\\\\\\\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\\\\\\\\n   264\\\\\\\\t|-------|--------|---------|\\\\\\\\n   265\\\\\\\\t| `by_processId_sequence` | `processId`, `sequence` | Canonical archive pagination |\\\\\\\\n   266\\\\\\\\t| `by_processId_finalizationKey` | `processId`, `finalizationKey` | Idempotency guard |\\\\\\\\n   267\\\\\\\\t| `by_projectId_processId_recordedAt` | `projectId`, `processId`, `recordedAt` | Project/process scoped diagnostics |\\\\\\\\n   268\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   269\\\\\\\\t`appendArchiveEntry` performs the final idempotency check and sequence assignment\\\\\\\\n   270\\\\\\\\tinside one Convex mutation. Fastify can preflight finalization keys, but Convex\\\\\\\\n   271\\\\\\\\towns the atomic guard.\\\\\\\\n   272\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   273\\\\\\\\t### Convex `archiveTurns`\\\\\\\\n   274\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   275\\\\\\\\t```typescript\\\\\\\\n   276\\\\\\\\texport const archiveTurnsTableFields = {\\\\\\\\n   277\\\\\\\\t  projectId: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   278\\\\\\\\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\\\\\\\\n   279\\\\\\\\t  turnId: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   280\\\\\\\\t  turnIndex: v.number(),\\\\\\\\n   281\\\\\\\\t  archiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\\\\\\\\n   282\\\\\\\\t  startedAt: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   283\\\\\\\\t  endedAt: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   284\\\\\\\\t  turnStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\\\\\\\\n   285\\\\\\\\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   286\\\\\\\\t  rebuiltAt: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   287\\\\\\\\t};\\\\\\\\n   288\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   289\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   290\\\\\\\\tIndexes:\\\\\\\\n   291\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   292\\\\\\\\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\\\\\\\\n   293\\\\\\\\t|-------|--------|---------|\\\\\\\\n   294\\\\\\\\t| `by_processId_turnId` | `processId`, `turnId` | Stable turn lookups across rebuilds |\\\\\\\\n   295\\\\\\\\t| `by_processId_turnIndex` | `processId`, `turnIndex` | Turn pagination and stable ordering |\\\\\\\\n   296\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   297\\\\\\\\tTurns are cached because bounded reads matter for long processes. The cache is\\\\\\\\n   298\\\\\\\\tnot canonical. `TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` must upsert turns by stable\\\\\\\\n   299\\\\\\\\t`turnId` (`${processId}:turn:${turnIndex}`) so derived-view provenance stays\\\\\\\\n   300\\\\\\\\tvalid across rebuilds.\\\\\\\\n   301\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   302\\\\\\\\t### Convex `derivedArchiveViews`\\\\\\\\n   303\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   304\\\\\\\\t```typescript\\\\\\\\n   305\\\\\\\\texport const derivedArchiveViewsTableFields = {\\\\\\\\n   306\\\\\\\\t  projectId: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   307\\\\\\\\t  processId: v.id('processes'),\\\\\\\\n   308\\\\\\\\t  viewKind: v.union(v.literal('turn_range'), v.literal('chunk_candidate')),\\\\\\\\n   309\\\\\\\\t  startTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   310\\\\\\\\t  endTurnIndex: v.union(v.number(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   311\\\\\\\\t  sourceTurnIds: v.array(v.string()),\\\\\\\\n   312\\\\\\\\t  sourceArchiveEntryIds: v.array(v.id('archiveEntries')),\\\\\\\\n   313\\\\\\\\t  title: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   314\\\\\\\\t  bodyText: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   315\\\\\\\\t  viewStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\\\\\\\\n   316\\\\\\\\t  degradationReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\\\\\\\\n   317\\\\\\\\t  updatedAt: v.string(),\\\\\\\\n   318\\\\\\\\t};\\\\\\\\n   319\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   320\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   321\\\\\\\\tIndexes:\\\\\\\\n   322\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   323\\\\\\\\t| Index | Fields | Purpose |\\\\\\\\n   324\\\\\\\\t|-------|--------|---------|\\\\\\\\n   325\\\\\\\\t| `by_processId_updatedAt` | `processId`, `updatedAt` | Derived-view reads |\\\\\\\\n   326\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   327\\\\\\\\tFor `turn_range`, `startTurnIndex` and `endTurnIndex` are required by Fastify\\\\\\\\n   328\\\\\\\\tvalidation before persistence. For `chunk_candidate`, the view must include\\\\\\\\n   329\\\\\\\\tsource turn ids and source archive entry ids; it must not include generated\\\\\\\\n   330\\\\\\\\tsummary content. Derived-view rows may be deleted and recreated from turns; this\\\\\\\\n   331\\\\\\\\tdoes not affect canonical archive entries.\\\\\\\\n   332\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   333\\\\\\\\tThe array fields in `archiveTurns` and `derivedArchiveViews` are intentionally\\\\\\\\n   334\\\\\\\\tbounded. Epic 7 limits turn rows to one process turn and derived views to small\\\\\\\\n   335\\\\\\\\tstructural groupings, not unbounded child lists. Long-process pagination stays\\\\\\\\n   336\\\\\\\\tat the archive-entry and turn level rather than trying to persist one giant\\\\\\\\n   337\\\\\\\\tderived record.\\\\\\\\n   338\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   339\\\\\\\\t## API Contracts\\\\\\\\n   340\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   341\\\\\\\\tShared contracts live in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts`.\\\\\\\\n   342\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   343\\\\\\\\t```typescript\\\\\\\\n   344\\\\\\\\texport type ArchiveEntryKind =\\\\\\\\n   345\\\\\\\\t  | 'user_message'\\\\\\\\n   346\\\\\\\\t  | 'model_message'\\\\\\\\n   347\\\\\\\\t  | 'reasoning'\\\\\\\\n   348\\\\\\\\t  | 'script_emission'\\\\\\\\n   349\\\\\\\\t  | 'tool_call'\\\\\\\\n   350\\\\\\\\t  | 'tool_result'\\\\\\\\n   351\\\\\\\\t  | 'process_event';\\\\\\\\n   352\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   353\\\\\\\\texport interface ArchiveEntry {\\\\\\\\n   354\\\\\\\\t  archiveEntryId: string;\\\\\\\\n   355\\\\\\\\t  projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   356\\\\\\\\t  processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   357\\\\\\\\t  entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\\\\\\\\n   358\\\\\\\\t  sequence: number;\\\\\\\\n   359\\\\\\\\t  lifecycleState: 'finalized';\\\\\\\\n   360\\\\\\\\t  finalizationKey: string;\\\\\\\\n   361\\\\\\\\t  sourceObjectId: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   362\\\\\\\\t  bodyText: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   363\\\\\\\\t  bodyData: { jsonText: string } | null;\\\\\\\\n   364\\\\\\\\t  bodyFormat: 'plain_text' | 'markdown' | 'structured' | 'none';\\\\\\\\n   365\\\\\\\\t  relatedArtifactVersionId: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   366\\\\\\\\t  relatedSourceProvenanceId: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   367\\\\\\\\t  relatedToolCallId: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   368\\\\\\\\t  entryStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\\\\\\\\n   369\\\\\\\\t  degradationReason: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   370\\\\\\\\t  recordedAt: string;\\\\\\\\n   371\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   372\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   373\\\\\\\\texport interface ArchivePage {\\\\\\\\n   374\\\\\\\\t  entries: ArchiveEntry[];\\\\\\\\n   375\\\\\\\\t  page: { cursor: string | null; nextCursor: string | null; hasMore: boolean };\\\\\\\\n   376\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   377\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   378\\\\\\\\texport interface DerivedTurn {\\\\\\\\n   379\\\\\\\\t  turnId: string;\\\\\\\\n   380\\\\\\\\t  processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   381\\\\\\\\t  turnIndex: number;\\\\\\\\n   382\\\\\\\\t  archiveEntryIds: string[];\\\\\\\\n   383\\\\\\\\t  startedAt: string;\\\\\\\\n   384\\\\\\\\t  endedAt: string;\\\\\\\\n   385\\\\\\\\t  turnStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\\\\\\\\n   386\\\\\\\\t  degradationReason: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   387\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   388\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   389\\\\\\\\texport interface DerivedArchiveView {\\\\\\\\n   390\\\\\\\\t  derivedViewId: string;\\\\\\\\n   391\\\\\\\\t  processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   392\\\\\\\\t  viewKind: 'turn_range' | 'chunk_candidate';\\\\\\\\n   393\\\\\\\\t  turnRange: { startIndex: number; endIndex: number } | null;\\\\\\\\n   394\\\\\\\\t  sourceTurnIds: string[];\\\\\\\\n   395\\\\\\\\t  sourceArchiveEntryIds: string[];\\\\\\\\n   396\\\\\\\\t  title: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   397\\\\\\\\t  bodyText: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   398\\\\\\\\t  viewStatus: 'ready' | 'degraded';\\\\\\\\n   399\\\\\\\\t  degradationReason: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   400\\\\\\\\t  updatedAt: string;\\\\\\\\n   401\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   402\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   403\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   404\\\\\\\\t### Routes\\\\\\\\n   405\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   406\\\\\\\\t| Operation | Method | Path | Service |\\\\\\\\n   407\\\\\\\\t|-----------|--------|------|---------|\\\\\\\\n   408\\\\\\\\t| Get process archive | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive` | `ArchiveReadService.getArchive` |\\\\\\\\n   409\\\\\\\\t| Get process turns | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/turns` | `TurnDerivationService.getTurns` |\\\\\\\\n   410\\\\\\\\t| Get derived archive views | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` |\\\\\\\\n   411\\\\\\\\t| Refresh derived archive views | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/archive/derived-views/refresh` | `DerivedArchiveViewService.refreshViews` |\\\\\\\\n   412\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   413\\\\\\\\tAll routes use existing actor resolution and `app.processAccessService` to\\\\\\\\n   414\\\\\\\\tenforce project/process access before archive services run.\\\\\\\\n   415\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   416\\\\\\\\t### Route Validation and Error Responses\\\\\\\\n   417\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   418\\\\\\\\t`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` should define these route schemas:\\\\\\\\n   419\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   420\\\\\\\\t- archive page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\\\\\\\\n   421\\\\\\\\t- turn page query: `cursor?: string | null`, `limit?: number`\\\\\\\\n   422\\\\\\\\t- derived-view refresh body: empty object for Epic 7\\\\\\\\n   423\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   424\\\\\\\\tRoute responses:\\\\\\\\n   425\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   426\\\\\\\\t| Route | 200 | Errors |\\\\\\\\n   427\\\\\\\\t|-------|-----|--------|\\\\\\\\n   428\\\\\\\\t| `GET /archive` | `ArchivePage` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\\\\\\\\n   429\\\\\\\\t| `GET /archive/turns` | `{ turns, page }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\\\\\\\\n   430\\\\\\\\t| `GET /archive/derived-views` | `{ views }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `422` |\\\\\\\\n   431\\\\\\\\t| `POST /archive/derived-views/refresh` | `{ views, refreshStatus }` | `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`, `422` |\\\\\\\\n   432\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   433\\\\\\\\tError codes:\\\\\\\\n   434\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   435\\\\\\\\t| Status | Code | Meaning |\\\\\\\\n   436\\\\\\\\t|--------|------|---------|\\\\\\\\n   437\\\\\\\\t| 401 | `UNAUTHENTICATED` | Actor is missing |\\\\\\\\n   438\\\\\\\\t| 403 | `PROJECT_FORBIDDEN` | Actor lacks project access |\\\\\\\\n   439\\\\\\\\t| 404 | `PROJECT_NOT_FOUND` | Project does not exist |\\\\\\\\n   440\\\\\\\\t| 404 | `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` | Process does not exist in project |\\\\\\\\n   441\\\\\\\\t| 409 | `ARCHIVE_DERIVATION_CONFLICT` | Derived-view refresh cannot safely reconcile with current archive state |\\\\\\\\n   442\\\\\\\\t| 422 | `INVALID_ARCHIVE_REQUEST` | Cursor, limit, or derived-view refresh request is invalid |\\\\\\\\n   443\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   444\\\\\\\\t## Service Interfaces\\\\\\\\n   445\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   446\\\\\\\\t```typescript\\\\\\\\n   447\\\\\\\\texport interface ArchiveFinalizationService {\\\\\\\\n   448\\\\\\\\t  appendFinalizedEntry(args: {\\\\\\\\n   449\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   450\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   451\\\\\\\\t    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\\\\\\\\n   452\\\\\\\\t    finalizationKey: string;\\\\\\\\n   453\\\\\\\\t    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   454\\\\\\\\t    bodyText?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   455\\\\\\\\t    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\\\\\\\\n   456\\\\\\\\t    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\\\\\\\\n   457\\\\\\\\t    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   458\\\\\\\\t    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   459\\\\\\\\t    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   460\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\\\\\\\\n   461\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   462\\\\\\\\t  appendFromProcessHistoryItem(args: {\\\\\\\\n   463\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   464\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   465\\\\\\\\t    historyItem: ProcessHistoryItem;\\\\\\\\n   466\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry | null>;\\\\\\\\n   467\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   468\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   469\\\\\\\\texport interface ArchiveReadService {\\\\\\\\n   470\\\\\\\\t  getArchive(args: {\\\\\\\\n   471\\\\\\\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\\\\\\\n   472\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   473\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   474\\\\\\\\t    cursor?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   475\\\\\\\\t    limit?: number;\\\\\\\\n   476\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\\\\\\\\n   477\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   478\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   479\\\\\\\\texport interface TurnDerivationService {\\\\\\\\n   480\\\\\\\\t  // Rebuilds cached turns by deterministic turnId rather than recreating\\\\\\\\n   481\\\\\\\\t  // opaque row ids, so downstream view provenance remains stable.\\\\\\\\n   482\\\\\\\\t  rebuildTurns(args: { projectId: string; processId: string }): Promise<DerivedTurn[]>;\\\\\\\\n   483\\\\\\\\t  getTurns(args: {\\\\\\\\n   484\\\\\\\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\\\\\\\n   485\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   486\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   487\\\\\\\\t    cursor?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   488\\\\\\\\t    limit?: number;\\\\\\\\n   489\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\\\\\\\\n   490\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   491\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   492\\\\\\\\texport interface DerivedArchiveViewService {\\\\\\\\n   493\\\\\\\\t  listViews(args: {\\\\\\\\n   494\\\\\\\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\\\\\\\n   495\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   496\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   497\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[] }>;\\\\\\\\n   498\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   499\\\\\\\\t  refreshViews(args: {\\\\\\\\n   500\\\\\\\\t    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n12:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '501,760p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n13:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md | sed -n '501,760p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"   501\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   502\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   503\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<{ views: DerivedArchiveView[]; refreshStatus: 'settled' | 'accepted' | 'degraded' }>;\\\\\\\\n   504\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   505\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   506\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   507\\\\\\\\t### PlatformStore Additions\\\\\\\\n   508\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   509\\\\\\\\t```typescript\\\\\\\\n   510\\\\\\\\texport interface PlatformStore {\\\\\\\\n   511\\\\\\\\t  appendArchiveEntry(args: {\\\\\\\\n   512\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   513\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   514\\\\\\\\t    entryKind: ArchiveEntryKind;\\\\\\\\n   515\\\\\\\\t    finalizationKey: string;\\\\\\\\n   516\\\\\\\\t    sourceObjectId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   517\\\\\\\\t    bodyText?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   518\\\\\\\\t    bodyData?: { jsonText: string } | null;\\\\\\\\n   519\\\\\\\\t    bodyFormat: ArchiveEntry['bodyFormat'];\\\\\\\\n   520\\\\\\\\t    relatedArtifactVersionId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   521\\\\\\\\t    relatedSourceProvenanceId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   522\\\\\\\\t    relatedToolCallId?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   523\\\\\\\\t    entryStatus?: 'ready' | 'degraded';\\\\\\\\n   524\\\\\\\\t    degradationReason?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   525\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<ArchiveEntry>;\\\\\\\\n   526\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   527\\\\\\\\t  listArchiveEntries(args: {\\\\\\\\n   528\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   529\\\\\\\\t    cursor?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   530\\\\\\\\t    limit: number;\\\\\\\\n   531\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<ArchivePage>;\\\\\\\\n   532\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   533\\\\\\\\t  upsertArchiveTurns(args: {\\\\\\\\n   534\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   535\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   536\\\\\\\\t    turns: DerivedTurn[];\\\\\\\\n   537\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<void>;\\\\\\\\n   538\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   539\\\\\\\\t  listArchiveTurns(args: {\\\\\\\\n   540\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   541\\\\\\\\t    cursor?: string | null;\\\\\\\\n   542\\\\\\\\t    limit: number;\\\\\\\\n   543\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<{ turns: DerivedTurn[]; page: ArchivePage['page'] }>;\\\\\\\\n   544\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   545\\\\\\\\t  replaceDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\\\\\\\\n   546\\\\\\\\t    projectId: string;\\\\\\\\n   547\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   548\\\\\\\\t    views: DerivedArchiveView[];\\\\\\\\n   549\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<void>;\\\\\\\\n   550\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   551\\\\\\\\t  listDerivedArchiveViews(args: {\\\\\\\\n   552\\\\\\\\t    processId: string;\\\\\\\\n   553\\\\\\\\t  }): Promise<DerivedArchiveView[]>;\\\\\\\\n   554\\\\\\\\t}\\\\\\\\n   555\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   556\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   557\\\\\\\\tConvex function validators should mirror these shapes directly. Fastify\\\\\\\\n   558\\\\\\\\tservices decide finalization, derivation, and refresh policy; `PlatformStore`\\\\\\\\n   559\\\\\\\\texposes only durable append/read/upsert/replace operations.\\\\\\\\n   560\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   561\\\\\\\\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\\\\\\\\n   562\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   563\\\\\\\\t### Flow 1: Capture Finalized Archive Entries\\\\\\\\n   564\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   565\\\\\\\\tThis flow covers the Story 1 primitive boundary behind AC-1.1 through AC-1.4.\\\\\\\\n   566\\\\\\\\tTrusted callers supply already-finalized archive-entry payloads to the durable\\\\\\\\n   567\\\\\\\\tappend/read primitive. Convex owns the canonical row shape, taxonomy\\\\\\\\n   568\\\\\\\\tvalidation, stable ordering, idempotency guard, related-id storage, and bounded\\\\\\\\n   569\\\\\\\\tprimitive reads.\\\\\\\\n   570\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   571\\\\\\\\t```mermaid\\\\\\\\n   572\\\\\\\\tsequenceDiagram\\\\\\\\n   573\\\\\\\\t    participant P as Trusted Caller\\\\\\\\n   574\\\\\\\\t    participant S as PlatformStore\\\\\\\\n   575\\\\\\\\t    participant X as Convex archiveEntries\\\\\\\\n   576\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   577\\\\\\\\t    P->>S: appendArchiveEntry(write)\\\\\\\\n   578\\\\\\\\t    Note over P,S: AC-1.1 finalized low-level entry payload\\\\\\\\n   579\\\\\\\\t    S->>X: appendArchiveEntry mutation\\\\\\\\n   580\\\\\\\\t    Note over S,X: AC-1.2/AC-1.3/AC-1.4 taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids\\\\\\\\n   581\\\\\\\\t    X-->>S: ArchiveEntry\\\\\\\\n   582\\\\\\\\t    S-->>P: ArchiveEntry\\\\\\\\n   583\\\\\\\\t```\\\\\\\\n   584\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   585\\\\\\\\t### Flow 2: Keep Live State Separate from Canonical Archive\\\\\\\\n   586\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   587\\\\\\\\tThis flow covers AC-2.1 through AC-2.3. Existing WebSocket upserts continue to\\\\\\\\n   588\\\\\\\\tserve active UI state through `process-live-normalizer.ts` and\\\\\\\\n   589\\\\\\\\t`process-live.ts`. Those live messages are not archive writes. Only completed\\\\\\\\n   590\\\\\\\\tobjects that reach a finalization point call `ArchiveFinalizationService`,\\\\\\\\n   591\\\\\\\\twhich maps finalized runtime/process objects into the Story 1 append primitive\\\\\\\\n   592\\\\\\\\texactly once.\\\\\\\\n   593\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   594\\\\\\\\tRetries are safe because every finalized object supplies a `finalizationKey`.\\\\\\\\n   595\\\\\\\\tExamples:\\\\\\\\n   596\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   597\\\\\\\\t- accepted user response: `response:${clientRequestId}`\\\\\\\\n   598\\\\\\\\t- runtime model message: `model:${sourceObjectId}`\\\\\\\\n   599\\\\\\\\t- tool call/result pair: `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:call` and `tool:${relatedToolCallId}:result`\\\\\\\\n   600\\\\\\\\t- process event: `event:${sourceObjectId}`\\\\\\\\n   601\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   602\\\\\\\\t### Flow 3: Read and Reopen Archive\\\\\\\\n   603\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   604\\\\\\\\tThis flow covers AC-3.1 through AC-3.4. The user reads archive entries through\\\\\\\\n   605\\\\\\\\tFastify routes under the existing process path. Archive reads do not depend on\\\\\\\\n   606\\\\\\\\tenvironment state or live WebSocket state. `ArchiveReadService` fetches one\\\\\\\\n   607\\\\\\\\tbounded page from Convex, applies route validation and access rules, and\\\\\\\\n   608\\\\\\\\treturns archive response rows for the client surface to render.\\\\\\\\n   609\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   610\\\\\\\\tThis flow owns displaying degraded entries already present in the response\\\\\\\\n   611\\\\\\\\tcontract. Deep artifact/source enrichment and lookup-failure degradation\\\\\\\\n   612\\\\\\\\tsemantics are added in Flow 6. Read-time degradation must not mutate the\\\\\\\\n   613\\\\\\\\tcanonical `archiveEntries` row unless the row itself was originally persisted\\\\\\\\n   614\\\\\\\\tas degraded.\\\\\\\\n   615\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   616\\\\\\\\t### Flow 4: Derive Turns\\\\\\\\n   617\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   618\\\\\\\\tThis flow covers AC-4.1 through AC-4.4. Turn derivation reads archive entries\\\\\\\\n   619\\\\\\\\tin ascending `sequence`, groups them deterministically, and writes cached turns\\\\\\\\n   620\\\\\\\\twhen refresh/rebuild is requested.\\\\\\\\n   621\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   622\\\\\\\\tGrouping rules:\\\\\\\\n   623\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   624\\\\\\\\t1. `user_message` starts a new turn.\\\\\\\\n   625\\\\\\\\t2. Entries before the first user message form turn `0` if they exist.\\\\\\\\n   626\\\\\\\\t3. `model_message`, `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`,\\\\\\\\n   627\\\\\\\\t   `tool_result`, and `process_event` attach to the active turn.\\\\\\\\n   628\\\\\\\\t  4. A `tool_result` with `relatedToolCallId` stays in the same turn as its\\\\\\\\n   629\\\\\\\\t   matching `tool_call` when both are present.\\\\\\\\n   630\\\\\\\\t  5. Degraded related context degrades the turn, not the archive entries.\\\\\\\\n   631\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   632\\\\\\\\tRebuild behavior is explicit: Epic 7 rebuilds turns on turn/derived-view read\\\\\\\\n   633\\\\\\\\tor explicit derived-view refresh, not on every archive append. Rebuild upserts by\\\\\\\\n   634\\\\\\\\tstable `turnId` and `turnIndex`.\\\\\\\\n   635\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   636\\\\\\\\t### Flow 5: Produce Minimal Structural Views\\\\\\\\n   637\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   638\\\\\\\\tThis flow covers AC-5.1 through AC-5.5. Structural views are generated from\\\\\\\\n   639\\\\\\\\tturns, not from raw live state. The first slice produces:\\\\\\\\n   640\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   641\\\\\\\\t- `turn_range`: one contiguous range of turn indexes with source entry ids\\\\\\\\n   642\\\\\\\\t- `chunk_candidate`: a candidate grouping over one or more turns for future\\\\\\\\n   643\\\\\\\\t  context-management work\\\\\\\\n   644\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   645\\\\\\\\tNeither view contains model-generated summaries. `bodyText`, when present, is a\\\\\\\\n   646\\\\\\\\tdeterministic label or structural note such as `Turns 4-8`.\\\\\\\\n   647\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   648\\\\\\\\t### Flow 6: Connect Provenance\\\\\\\\n   649\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   650\\\\\\\\tThis flow covers AC-6.1 through AC-6.3. Archive entries store nullable related\\\\\\\\n   651\\\\\\\\tids. Building on the Flow 3 archive read surface, read services enrich when\\\\\\\\n   652\\\\\\\\tpossible:\\\\\\\\n   653\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   654\\\\\\\\t- artifact context through `PlatformStore.listArtifactVersions` or a targeted\\\\\\\\n   655\\\\\\\\t  artifact-version read helper\\\\\\\\n   656\\\\\\\\t- source context through Epic 6 `sourceProvenance` reads\\\\\\\\n   657\\\\\\\\t- tool context through `relatedToolCallId`\\\\\\\\n   658\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   659\\\\\\\\tIf a related record is unavailable, the entry remains visible. This flow owns\\\\\\\\n   660\\\\\\\\tthe artifact/source lookup-failure degradation semantics: the archive entry\\\\\\\\n   661\\\\\\\\tstatus becomes `degraded` for the read response, or an enriched response\\\\\\\\n   662\\\\\\\\tincludes degraded related-context metadata without mutating the stored\\\\\\\\n   663\\\\\\\\tcanonical entry. Story 3 remains responsible for rendering that response\\\\\\\\n   664\\\\\\\\tstate to the user.\\\\\\\\n   665\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   666\\\\\\\\t### Flow 7: Return Later and Bound Long Reads\\\\\\\\n   667\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   668\\\\\\\\tThis flow covers AC-7.1 through AC-7.3. Archive entries, turns, and derived\\\\\\\\n   669\\\\\\\\tviews are durable or rebuildable from durable entries. Reads use cursor\\\\\\\\n   670\\\\\\\\tpagination with default limits:\\\\\\\\n   671\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   672\\\\\\\\t- archive entries: default 100, max 200\\\\\\\\n   673\\\\\\\\t- turns: default 50, max 100\\\\\\\\n   674\\\\\\\\t- derived views: default 50\\\\\\\\n   675\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   676\\\\\\\\tA derived-view read or rebuild failure does not block archive reads. Routes\\\\\\\\n   677\\\\\\\\treturn degraded view state for derived failures and keep archive entries\\\\\\\\n   678\\\\\\\\tavailable.\\\\\\\\n   679\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   680\\\\\\\\t## Implementation Chunks\\\\\\\\n   681\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   682\\\\\\\\t| Chunk | Story | Scope | ACs | Primary Tests |\\\\\\\\n   683\\\\\\\\t|-------|-------|-------|-----|---------------|\\\\\\\\n   684\\\\\\\\t| 0 | Foundation | Contracts, Convex schema, fixtures, error codes, compatibility mapping skeletons | All support | Relevant sections: API Contracts, Data Model. Non-TC: archive contract vocabulary and finalized-only schema test |\\\\\\\\n   685\\\\\\\\t| 1 | Archive persistence | Append/read entries, taxonomy, ordering, idempotency, related ids | AC-1.x | Relevant sections: Flow 1, Data Model. Non-TC: atomic sequence assignment and primitive idempotency |\\\\\\\\n   686\\\\\\\\t| 2 | Finalization boundary | Completion hooks, live/archive separation, retry idempotency | AC-2.x | Relevant sections: Flow 2, Service Interfaces. Non-TC: live-history separation, compatibility mapping decision |\\\\\\\\n   687\\\\\\\\t| 3 | Archive read/reopen | Routes, access controls, empty state, bounded page contract, environment-loss reads, degraded-entry display | AC-3.x | Relevant sections: Flow 3, Route Validation. Non-TC: invalid archive request handling |\\\\\\\\n   688\\\\\\\\t| 4 | Turn derivation | Deterministic grouping, cached rebuild, degraded turns | AC-4.x | Relevant sections: Flow 4, Data Model. Non-TC: turn-zero grouping, rebuild stability |\\\\\\\\n   689\\\\\\\\t| 5 | Structural derived views | `turn_range`, `chunk_candidate`, refresh, degradation | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Route Validation. Non-TC: no generated summary body, stale/rebuilt derived views |\\\\\\\\n   690\\\\\\\\t| 6 | Provenance coherence | Artifact/source enrichment and related-record lookup degradation semantics | AC-6.x | Relevant sections: Flow 6, API Contracts. Non-TC: none |\\\\\\\\n   691\\\\\\\\t| 7 | Reopen/bounded reads | Reload behavior, derived failures, long-process pagination hardening | AC-7.x | Relevant sections: Flow 7, Route Validation. Non-TC: none |\\\\\\\\n   692\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   693\\\\\\\\t## Verification\\\\\\\\n   694\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   695\\\\\\\\t| Script | Command | Use |\\\\\\\\n   696\\\\\\\\t|--------|---------|-----|\\\\\\\\n   697\\\\\\\\t| `red-verify` | `pnpm run red-verify` | After skeleton and Red tests |\\\\\\\\n   698\\\\\\\\t| `verify` | `pnpm run verify` | Standard development gate |\\\\\\\\n   699\\\\\\\\t| `green-verify` | `pnpm run green-verify` | After implementation passes tests |\\\\\\\\n   700\\\\\\\\t| `verify-all` | `pnpm run verify-all` | Story/Epic completion |\\\\\\\\n   701\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   702\\\\\\\\t## Deferred Items\\\\\\\\n   703\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   704\\\\\\\\t| Item | Related AC | Reason Deferred | Future Work |\\\\\\\\n   705\\\\\\\\t|------|------------|-----------------|-------------|\\\\\\\\n   706\\\\\\\\t| Historical migration/backfill from `processHistoryItems` | A7 | Epic 7 starts forward canonical archive and compatibility bridge | Later migration if needed |\\\\\\\\n   707\\\\\\\\t| Model-generated summaries | Scope, AC-5.x | Structural views only | Later context-management epic |\\\\\\\\n   708\\\\\\\\t| Model-specific prompt packing | Scope | Not required for archive truth | Later context-management epic |\\\\\\\\n   709\\\\\\\\t| External-source archive integration | Scope | Epic 6/7 sequence is repository-focused | Later source-integration work |\\\\\\\\n   710\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   711\\\\\\\\t## Resolved Implementation Decisions\\\\\\\\n   712\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   713\\\\\\\\t| Decision | Applied In |\\\\\\\\n   714\\\\\\\\t|----------|------------|\\\\\\\\n   715\\\\\\\\t| `relatedSourceProvenanceId` is implemented as the stable Epic 6 provenance identifier and stays string-shaped in shared contracts unless cross-table typing becomes frictionless. | Chunk 6 |\\\\\\\\n   716\\\\\\\\t| Turn cache rebuild happens on turn/derived-view read or explicit refresh, not on every archive append. | Chunk 4 |\\\\\\\\n   717\\\\\\\\t| Compatibility mapping does not publish archive entries back into the live history stream. Live history publisher remains unchanged. | Chunk 2 |\\\\\\\\n   718\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   719\\\\\\\\t## Self-Review Checklist\\\\\\\\n   720\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   721\\\\\\\\t- [x] Every Epic 7 AC has a module owner.\\\\\\\\n   722\\\\\\\\t- [x] Every Epic 7 Tech Design Question is answered.\\\\\\\\n   723\\\\\\\\t- [x] Canonical archive and live upserts stay separate.\\\\\\\\n   724\\\\\\\\t- [x] Turns and derived views are rebuildable, not canonical.\\\\\\\\n   725\\\\\\\\t- [x] Structural views exclude generated summaries.\\\\\\\\n   726\\\\\\\\t- [x] Verification commands use project scripts.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n14:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md | sed -n '1,220p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n15:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md | sed -n '1,220p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"     1\\\\\\\\t# Test Plan: Epic 7 Archive and Derived Views\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\t## Purpose\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\tThis test plan maps every Epic 7 test condition to planned tests. It verifies\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\tcanonical archive append/read behavior, finalization boundaries, archive read\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\tsurfaces, turn derivation, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, and\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\tdegraded reads.\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\tRelated design: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md`\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\t## Test Strategy\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\t### Test Layers\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t| Layer | Files | Purpose |\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\t|-------|-------|---------|\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\t| Convex service tests | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts`, `convex/archiveTurns.test.ts`, `convex/derivedArchiveViews.test.ts` | Durable append/read, sequence, idempotency, cached projections |\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t| Fastify service/API tests | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | Auth/access, finalization policy, archive reads, derivation, degraded states |\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\t| Client service tests | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts`, `tests/service/client/archive-turns-section.test.ts`, `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` | User-visible archive, turn, structural-view, empty, pagination, and degraded states |\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\t| Existing live/process tests | `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/process-execution-orchestrator.test.ts` | Ensure live upserts remain separate from archive finalization |\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\t### Scope Boundaries\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\t| Story | Owns | Does Not Prove |\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\t|-------|------|----------------|\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\t| 1 Archive persistence | Convex archive-entry primitive, taxonomy, sequence ordering, idempotency guard, related-id round-trip | Service finalization hooks, archive route/UI, read-time artifact/source enrichment |\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\t| 2 Finalization boundary | Service-level proof that completed live objects append exactly once and partial/delta objects do not append | Primitive storage mechanics beyond Story 1 contract, browser archive read surface |\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\t| 3 Archive read/reopen | Authenticated route/UI, reload/environment-loss reads, access checks, bounded page contract, displaying degraded entries already present in the response | Deep artifact/source provenance enrichment or lookup-failure degradation semantics |\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\t| 6 Provenance coherence | Artifact/source enrichment and per-entry lookup-failure degradation semantics | Replacing Story 3 route/UI, access, reload, or bounded-page behavior |\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\t### Mock Boundaries\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\t| Boundary | Mock? | Notes |\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\t|----------|-------|-------|\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\t| Artifact/source enrichment services | Yes in Story 6 archive read tests | Mock unavailable related context to verify per-entry degradation |\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\t| Environment/provider runtime | Yes | Finalization tests use completed/interrupted fake runtime objects |\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\t| Convex in route tests | Existing fake/in-memory PlatformStore pattern | Route tests exercise Fastify services without live Convex |\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\t| Internal derivation helpers | No | Test via `TurnDerivationService` and `DerivedArchiveViewService` |\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\t| Client API calls | Yes | Client tests mock fetch/API layer only |\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\t## TC to Test Mapping\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\t| TC | Test File | Test Description | Coverage Notes |\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\t|----|-----------|------------------|----------------|\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.1a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.1a appends finalized user_message entry through primitive` | Trusted caller payload persists as canonical `user_message` row |\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.1b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.1b appends finalized model_message entry through primitive` | Trusted caller payload persists as canonical `model_message` row |\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.1c | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.1c appends finalized process_event entry through primitive` | Trusted caller payload persists as canonical `process_event` row |\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.2a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.2a accepts required archive entry kinds` | All seven kinds accepted |\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.2b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.2b rejects unsupported archive entry kind` | Invalid kind creates no row |\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.3a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.3a reads entries in stable sequence order` | Ascending sequence |\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.3b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.3b same timestamp entries remain deterministic` | Sequence breaks timestamp ties |\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.4a | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.4a round-trips related ids on archive row` | Related artifact/source/tool ids return unchanged from canonical row |\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t| TC-1.4b | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | `TC-1.4b archive row remains readable without related-record lookup` | Primitive read does not require enrichment |\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.1a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.1a raw streaming delta excluded from archive` | Delta object never calls append |\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.2a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.2a interrupted model output excluded` | Interrupted object ignored |\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.2b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.2b incomplete tool result excluded` | Tool result without finalization ignored |\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.3a completed live object archived once through finalization service` | Finalization service appends one canonical entry |\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\t| TC-2.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` | `TC-2.3b replayed completion does not duplicate entry through service boundary` | Retried completion does not duplicate archive append |\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\t| TC-3.1a | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | `TC-3.1a archive entries visible` | Client renders finalized entries |\\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\t| TC-3.1b | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | `TC-3.1b empty archive state visible` | Empty state rendered |\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\t| TC-3.2a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.2a archive survives reload` | GET archive reads durable state |\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\t| TC-3.2b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.2b archive survives environment loss` | Environment absent does not affect archive read |\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\t| TC-3.3a | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | `TC-3.3a unauthorized archive read blocked` | 40