lization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:759:        evidence: \\\"`ProcessHistoryCompatService` derives bridged `user_message` keys from `historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:61-68`), while `ProcessResponseService` archives the same accepted response under `response:${clientRequestId}` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:153-168`). `ArchiveFinalizationService` only short-circuits when an existing row with the same `sourceObjectId` is already present (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:70-79`), so the opposite order still duplicates. I reproduced this with `corepack pnpm exec tsx` by calling `submitProcessResponse()` -> `appendFromProcessHistoryItem()` -> `respond()`; the archive then contained two `user_message` rows for the same `sourceObjectId`: `response:process-archive-finalization:history-response-1` and `response:req-archive-4`.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:772:        id: \\\"story2-green-verify-format-failure\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:775:        evidence: \\\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` exited 1 in `format:check` because Biome would reformat the constructor type wrapping in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:15-17`. The story gate therefore does not pass in the current workspace.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:799:        evidence: \\\"`ProcessHistoryCompatService` derives bridged `user_message` keys from `historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:61-68`), while `ProcessResponseService` archives the same accepted response under `response:${clientRequestId}` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:153-168`). `ArchiveFinalizationService` only short-circuits when an existing row with the same `sourceObjectId` is already present (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:70-79`), so the opposite order still duplicates. I reproduced this with `corepack pnpm exec tsx` by calling `submitProcessResponse()` -> `appendFromProcessHistoryItem()` -> `respond()`; the archive then contained two `user_message` rows for the same `sourceObjectId`: `response:process-archive-finalization:history-response-1` and `response:req-archive-4`.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:812:        id: \\\"story2-green-verify-format-failure\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:815:        evidence: \\\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` exited 1 in `format:check` because Biome would reformat the constructor type wrapping in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:15-17`. The story gate therefore does not pass in the current workspace.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:864:        command: \\\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:867:        command: \\\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:876:      - \\\"Focused story tests pass, and standalone lint/typecheck/build pass; the only gate failure I observed was the Biome format check inside `green-verify`.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:968:    reviewScopeSummary: \\\"Reviewed Story 2 against its story/spec/test-plan, then verified the finalization seam across `ArchiveFinalizationService`, the user-response and execution hooks, process-history compatibility, and the Story 2 server/client tests. I also ran the configured story and epic gates plus an ad hoc runtime reproduction of execution-result archiving.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:976:        evidence: \\\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\\\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\\\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\\\\\"runtime-model-1\\\\\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\\\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\\\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:991:        evidence: \\\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\\\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\\\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\\\\\"runtime-model-1\\\\\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\\\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\\\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:1017:        command: \\\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:1020:        command: \\\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:1029:      - \\\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but the current Story 2 tests miss the identity mismatch because TC-2.3b asserts the provider-supplied `runtime-model-1` ID rather than the stored history row returned by `appendProcessHistoryItem`.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:1160:Latest note highlight: After verifier returns, accept only if outcome is pass, no open findings remain, Story 2 coverage includes TC-2.1a through TC-2.3b plus live/archive separation and compatibility mapping, and `corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:1165:- sequence=12; actionSequence=11; createdAt=2026-05-05T04:16:46.544Z; note=\\\"After quick-fix returns, run verification focused on the fixed user_message bridge finalizationKey finding plus TC-2.3b and compatibility mapping evidence before considering accept-story.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:1168:- sequence=24; actionSequence=23; createdAt=2026-05-05T04:33:56.485Z; note=\\\"After verifier returns, accept only if outcome is pass, no open findings remain, 