{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_98","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The derived-view pagination change is only partially propagated: shared contracts, route/schema wiring, the derived-view service, PlatformStore implementations, and several test doubles no longer agree on the `listDerivedArchiveViews` request/response shape.\",\"Turn and derived-view cache behavior now diverges between the in-memory test store and the Convex production store, so cross-story reopen behavior is not being validated against the real persistence path.\",\"Archive capture, turn derivation, and derived-view surfaces are conceptually aligned around archive truth, but the default execution path that feeds the archive is still a canned runtime-audit script rather than real process-specific execution.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design says turn and derived-view rebuilds happen on read from canonical archive data; the current services only rebuild when the cached first page is empty, which is weaker than the documented contract.\",\"The architecture expects Fastify pagination contracts to match store and durable-layer contracts end to end; the current derived-view rollout breaks that consistency and fails the type gate before tests can run.\",\"Canonical archive truth is supposed to preserve finalized process work, but the default production executor still synthesizes archive entries from a hard-coded audit payload.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run verify-all` fails in `typecheck`, so none of the Epic 7 service, client, integration, or e2e tests actually execute to green.\",\"The added Story 6/7 tests around detached-source degradation and bounded derived-view pages improve intended coverage, but they currently provide no passing evidence because the build is broken first.\",\"Static inspection found a production-only stale-cache path that the in-memory tests mask, so even a later green test run should explicitly verify Convex-backed reopen/read behavior.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The production app wires `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default, and that service's default payload factory emits a synthetic integrated runtime-audit script that fabricates `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission` archive entries.\",\"`InMemoryPlatformStore` deletes cached turns and derived views on archive append/patch, but `ConvexPlatformStore` does not, so production can serve stale derived data even though the primary test store self-heals.\",\"No equivalent fake adapter was found in the archive read routes themselves; the material non-real execution paths are the canned script executor and the test-only cache invalidation behavior.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC7-DERIVED-VIEW-PAGINATION-ROLLUP\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Derived-view pagination refactor is incomplete and breaks the epic gate\",\"evidence\":\"Running `corepack pnpm run verify-all` fails in `typecheck` before any Epic 7 tests run. The current rollout leaves `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService` and multiple store/test implementations disagreeing about the `listDerivedArchiveViews` shape: TypeScript reports `'cursor' does not exist in type '{ processId: string; }'`, `'views' does not exist on type 'DerivedArchiveView[]'`, plus contract failures in `tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts`, and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC7-STale-DERIVED-CACHE-PRODUCTION\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Convex production reads can return stale turns and derived views after new archive entries arrive\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` rebuilds only when the first cached page is empty, and `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` now does the same. In production, `ConvexPlatformStore.appendArchiveEntry` and `patchArchiveEntry` only write archive rows; they never clear `archiveTurns` or `derivedArchiveViews`. By contrast, `InMemoryPlatformStore` explicitly deletes those caches on append/patch and after turn upserts. After the first successful rebuild, later archive appends in Convex can leave `/archive/turns` and `/archive/derived-views` stale indefinitely until an explicit refresh.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC7-SYNTHETIC-ARCHIVE-PRODUCTION-PATH\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"The default production archive capture path still archives a canned runtime-audit script, not real process execution\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` when no override is injected. The default `ScriptExecutionService` payload factory always returns `buildIntegratedRuntimeAuditPayload`, whose hard-coded TypeScript module writes a runtime report and emits synthetic archive entries for `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission`. That means the live production path feeding Epic 7 is still a placeholder execution program rather than real process-specific work.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Rerun `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` after finishing the derived-view pagination rollout; the current review could not observe any post-typecheck test results.\",\"Decide whether the integrated runtime-audit payload is an accepted temporary production path or a release blocker for Epic 7 shipping.\",\"After fixing the cache policy, verify turn and derived-view reopen behavior against the real Convex store, not only `InMemoryPlatformStore`.\"],\"gateResult\":\"fail\"}"}}
