w wrappers require the shared API key and preserve archive rows\nAssertionError: expected [ { …(11) } ] to deeply equal { Object (views, page) }\n\n- Expected:\n{\n  \"page\": {\n    \"cursor\": null,\n    \"hasMore\": false,\n    \"nextCursor\": null,\n  },\n  \"views\": [\n    ObjectContaining {\n      \"derivedViewId\": \"process-archive-1:derived-view:turn_range:0-0\",\n    },\n  ],\n}\n\n+ Received:\n[\n  {\n    \"bodyText\": \"Turn 0\",\n    \"degradationReason\": null,\n    \"derivedViewId\": \"process-archive-1:derived-view:turn_range:0-0\",\n    \"processId\": \"process-archive-1\",\n    \"sourceArchiveEntryIds\": [\n      \"archiveEntries:1\",\n    ],\n    \"sourceTurnIds\": [\n      \"process-archive-1:turn:0\",\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Turn 0\",\n    \"turnRange\": {\n      \"endIndex\": 0,\n      \"startIndex\": 0,\n    },\n    \"updatedAt\": \"2026-05-01T10:11:10.000Z\",\n    \"viewKind\": \"turn_range\",\n    \"viewStatus\": \"ready\",\n  },\n]\n\n ❯ convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:809:25\n    807|     });\n    808|\n    809|     expect(storedViews).toEqual({\n       |                         ^\n    810|       views: [\n    811|         expect.objectContaining({\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[2/2]⎯\n\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  2 failed | 8 passed (10)\n   Start at  07:46:34\n   Duration  195ms (transform 44ms, setup 0ms, import 64ms, tests 12ms, environment 0ms)\n\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_168","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Archive entry reads and turn derivation are mostly intact, but the derived-view slice is currently broken: `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` passed 15/15 and `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` passed 8/8, while `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` now fails 6 of 7 cases with 500s.\",\"The archive/turn/view layers no longer react consistently to provenance-only degradation. `/archive` re-enriches entries per read, but cached turns/views can stay stale after source detachment or related-context loss.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"A partial derived-view pagination refactor drifted across layers. `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService` expects paged stored-view reads, but lower store/Convex seams and several callers still assume the older array-returning contract.\",\"Derived projections are only invalidated on archive writes. Source/artifact state changes do not invalidate or recompute `archiveTurns` / derived views, so the rebuildable-projection contract no longer matches the archive read path's degraded-state behavior.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Archive append/read, access checks, and turn derivation still have meaningful coverage: `archive-api.test.ts` passed 15/15 and `turn-derivation.test.ts` passed 8/8 when run directly.\",\"Derived-view coverage is red. `derived-archive-view.test.ts` fails TC-5.1a, TC-5.2a/5.3a/5.3b, the degraded-on-reopen scenario, TC-7.1b, bounded paging, and the derived-view cache invalidation scenario.\",\"Epic 7 is not green end-to-end because Story 5/7 behavior is down and the turn/view degraded-state contract is inconsistent with Story 6 provenance degradation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The live derived-view read path is materially broken right now. `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` returns 500s for the GET `/archive/derived-views` scenarios, so the structural-view surface is not usable.\",\"Turn and derived-view caches are not refreshed when only related provenance changes. A source detachment can change `/archive` output immediately while `/archive/turns` and cached derived views keep serving pre-detachment readiness.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derived-view read path is broken by a partially applied pagination contract change\",\"evidence\":\"`corepack pnpm run typecheck` reports `apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts(254,48)` because `listAllStoredViews` is still calling `platformStore.listDerivedArchiveViews({ processId })` while the new signature requires paging, and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts(417,61)` / `tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts(341,5)` show callers still returning arrays instead of `{ views, page }`. Running `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` now yields 6 failing 500s, and `corepack pnpm vitest run convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` still fails the derived-view primitive expectations.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\",\"tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts\",\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-5.2\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-07-02\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Cached turns and derived views do not re-derive when provenance degrades after the archive is written\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultArchiveReadService` re-enriches archive entries on every read (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:52-65` plus `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-entry-enrichment.ts:10-152`), but `DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` only rebuilds when the cached turn page is empty (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:87-98`). I reproduced this by building turns, detaching the linked source attachment, and calling `getTurns` again; the second response still returned the original `ready` turn. The derived-view service follows the same cache-first pattern, so reopen behavior can diverge between `/archive`, `/archive/turns`, and cached derived views after source detachment or provenance degradation.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-entry-enrichment.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Both named gates are failed, but neither completed a clean full sweep: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` stopped immediately in `format:check` on `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts`, so the remaining lint/build/integration stages were not reached in a passing run.\",\"The provenance-staleness regression was reproduced manually at the service layer; there is no current automated regression test covering cache refresh after source detachment.\"],\"gateResult\":\"fail\"}"}}
